WEBVTT

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.142 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.631 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:43.385 line:80%
I found you.

00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:45.846 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:52.519 line:80%
This is bad.

00:01:02.446 --> 00:01:04.448 line:80%
[♪ uplifting song playing]

00:01:13.207 --> 00:01:14.833 line:80%
Why are you…

00:01:15.918 --> 00:01:17.252 line:80%
I'm just copying you.

00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:21.799 line:80%
I have a habit of copying other people.

00:01:24.635 --> 00:01:25.719 line:80%
[sighs]

00:01:26.387 --> 00:01:29.598 line:80%
-[stammers] But I can't breathe…
-Oh.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.101 line:80%
Sorry.

00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:33.727 line:80%
[chuckles awkwardly, clears throat]

00:01:34.311 --> 00:01:37.272 line:80%
You said you hug people
you're happy to see.

00:01:44.697 --> 00:01:45.698 line:80%
[♪ song ends]

00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:48.367 line:20%
EPISODE 7

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.743 line:20%
[indicator clicking]

00:01:49.827 --> 00:01:51.495 line:20%
[driver clicks tongue, sighs]

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.584 line:20%
[car thuds]

00:02:08.262 --> 00:02:09.805 line:20%
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

00:02:11.348 --> 00:02:12.349 line:20%
[Chan clears throat]

00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:24.695 line:80%
We're here.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.531 line:80%
Sir?

00:02:28.365 --> 00:02:29.408 line:80%
Yes?

00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:37.541 line:80%
Can you open the trunk?

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:40.461 line:80%
Just keep riding this to SHIM.
Mr. Park will be waiting.

00:02:45.716 --> 00:02:46.717 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:02:49.178 --> 00:02:50.179 line:80%
[sighs]

00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:55.434 line:80%
Ah.

00:02:56.185 --> 00:02:57.353 line:80%
Yes, Mr. Yeon.

00:02:57.936 --> 00:02:59.104 line:80%
Producer Ben?

00:02:59.188 --> 00:03:00.606 line:80%
[Yeon] <i>He just informed me</i>

00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:02.775 line:80%
<i>that the collaboration project</i>
<i>will resume.</i>

00:03:05.861 --> 00:03:06.987 line:80%
Huh?

00:03:08.656 --> 00:03:10.115 line:80%
[Haran gasps, chuckles]

00:03:10.199 --> 00:03:12.701 line:80%
[Yeon] <i>The animation team</i>
<i>will return to Korea soon.</i>

00:03:12.785 --> 00:03:14.995 line:80%
All right. That's good.

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:16.955 line:80%
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[chuckles]

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.169 line:80%
[grunts, pants]

00:03:22.252 --> 00:03:23.420 line:80%
[Manjae] My roommate!

00:03:24.254 --> 00:03:25.839 line:80%
[Chan] Oh. Mr. Park!

00:03:26.382 --> 00:03:27.758 line:80%
Mr. Park.

00:03:27.841 --> 00:03:29.551 line:80%
How have you been?

00:03:29.635 --> 00:03:31.053 line:80%
Sorry, I couldn't call you.

00:03:33.389 --> 00:03:34.682 line:80%
You're here, so it's fine.

00:03:34.765 --> 00:03:37.059 line:80%
Why are you standing out here in the cold?

00:03:37.142 --> 00:03:38.811 line:80%
You didn't know when I'd get here.

00:03:38.894 --> 00:03:40.688 line:80%
I just came out 10 seconds ago.

00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:44.566 line:80%
Goodness. But look at you…

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:48.779 line:80%
You must have been through a lot.
You look so gaunt.

00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:50.406 line:80%
Do I?

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:51.949 line:80%
[groans] That's awful.

00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:53.659 line:80%
I should get prettier now.

00:03:53.742 --> 00:03:55.536 line:80%
[chuckles, stutters]

00:03:55.619 --> 00:03:57.454 line:80%
You didn't forget your meds, right?

00:03:57.538 --> 00:03:59.373 line:80%
And your cardiac enzyme levels?

00:04:00.124 --> 00:04:01.792 line:80%
It's cold. Let's go inside.

00:04:01.875 --> 00:04:05.045 line:80%
-Genius, Chan is here. Come on in.
-[Genius barks]

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:07.297 line:80%
-It's cold.
-Are you running away?

00:04:07.381 --> 00:04:08.674 line:80%
Mr. Park!

00:04:09.341 --> 00:04:11.593 line:80%
-[exclaims] Genius!
-[whines]

00:04:11.677 --> 00:04:12.720 line:80%
Genius.

00:04:12.803 --> 00:04:14.638 line:80%
-[♪ pleasant music playing]
-[whines]

00:04:14.722 --> 00:04:17.766 line:80%
Hey, Genius.
Aren't you going to show me your face?

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.601 line:80%
Hey, Grouchy.

00:04:19.685 --> 00:04:22.688 line:80%
You were waiting for Chan the whole time.
Are you protesting?

00:04:22.771 --> 00:04:24.857 line:80%
[sighs] Leave him.

00:04:25.357 --> 00:04:27.484 line:80%
He's sour because you left
without telling him.

00:04:27.985 --> 00:04:29.403 line:80%
Go upstairs. You must be tired.

00:04:31.739 --> 00:04:32.740 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:04:32.823 --> 00:04:34.700 line:80%
[groans]

00:04:34.783 --> 00:04:36.160 line:80%
[sighs]

00:04:37.369 --> 00:04:38.370 line:80%
[sighs]

00:04:46.253 --> 00:04:47.254 line:80%
[wooden thud]

00:04:47.338 --> 00:04:49.673 line:80%
Oh… Yes, Mr. Park. Come in.

00:04:51.717 --> 00:04:52.718 line:80%
[grunts softly]

00:04:53.344 --> 00:04:54.345 line:80%
-[Genius barks]
-Oh?

00:04:55.971 --> 00:04:58.140 line:80%
-Genius. [chuckles]
-[whines]

00:04:58.223 --> 00:05:01.310 line:80%
Want to sleep with me today?
Hmm? [chuckles]

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.356 line:80%
Dogs should sleep at this hour.

00:05:05.981 --> 00:05:06.982 line:80%
Hmm?

00:05:07.483 --> 00:05:08.609 line:80%
Me?

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.279 line:80%
I have a lot on my mind.

00:05:13.447 --> 00:05:18.410 line:80%
Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

00:05:19.662 --> 00:05:22.539 line:80%
That's all I wanted for her,

00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:25.626 line:80%
but what do I do now?

00:05:26.794 --> 00:05:27.836 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:31.382 line:80%
I want her to be happy beside me,

00:05:34.426 --> 00:05:36.970 line:80%
and I want her to be happy because of me.

00:05:38.138 --> 00:05:39.848 line:80%
I keep getting greedy.

00:05:41.016 --> 00:05:43.102 line:80%
IF IT'S OKAY WITH YOU, YOU CAN TALK TO ME

00:05:43.185 --> 00:05:47.231 line:80%
<i>The fact that I was fake,</i>
<i>and the reason I became a fake…</i>

00:05:48.023 --> 00:05:53.696 line:80%
<i>The fact that I lived</i>
<i>while he died from that accident…</i>

00:05:57.533 --> 00:06:02.121 line:80%
<i>I keep wanting to do as I want</i>

00:06:03.247 --> 00:06:04.665 line:80%
<i>as if I'm clueless to all that.</i>

00:06:07.126 --> 00:06:08.794 line:80%
<i>Until I go back,</i>

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.507 line:80%
<i>if I play dumb and be greedy,</i>

00:06:14.717 --> 00:06:15.968 line:80%
<i>would that be wrong?</i>

00:06:16.969 --> 00:06:18.595 line:80%
[wind whooshing]

00:06:18.679 --> 00:06:21.890 line:80%
-[leaves rustling]
-[bird chirping]

00:06:21.974 --> 00:06:23.892 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:06:23.976 --> 00:06:25.644 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:06:25.728 --> 00:06:27.313 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Here's today's dress code.</i>

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.732 line:80%
<i>Comfy shoes and warm clothes.</i>

00:06:30.524 --> 00:06:31.608 line:80%
<i>See you later.</i>

00:06:31.692 --> 00:06:33.610 line:80%
I can't travel too far today.

00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:36.280 line:80%
CLOSED DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

00:06:36.363 --> 00:06:37.364 line:80%
Oh?

00:06:38.532 --> 00:06:39.575 line:80%
Hmm?

00:06:40.159 --> 00:06:41.994 line:80%
-[lively chatter]
-Mr. Park…

00:06:43.078 --> 00:06:44.663 line:80%
-Oh! Ms. Song.
-Ms. Song.

00:06:44.747 --> 00:06:46.248 line:80%
-Hey.
-Hello.

00:06:46.332 --> 00:06:47.333 line:80%
[Haran] What are you all doing…

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.501 line:80%
Ben, when did you get here?

00:06:49.585 --> 00:06:50.586 line:80%
Have you been well?

00:06:50.669 --> 00:06:53.130 line:80%
I visited as soon as I arrived,
and now I'm trapped.

00:06:53.213 --> 00:06:54.214 line:80%
[laughter]

00:06:54.298 --> 00:06:56.633 line:80%
We came when we saw Seunggyu's photo
in our group chat.

00:06:56.717 --> 00:06:59.511 line:80%
I wanted to get the coffee
you bought us last time,

00:06:59.595 --> 00:07:01.930 line:80%
-and I saw that Chan was here.
-[chuckles softly]

00:07:02.014 --> 00:07:05.768 line:80%
As soon as I saw the photo,
I rushed over with my sheet mask still on.

00:07:05.851 --> 00:07:08.187 line:80%
Things worked out,
so he's staying for two months.

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.563 line:80%
Isn't that great?

00:07:09.647 --> 00:07:11.357 line:80%
Right…

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:12.524 line:80%
[toy] <i>Let's play.</i>

00:07:12.608 --> 00:07:13.776 line:80%
<i>Let's play.</i>

00:07:13.859 --> 00:07:16.403 line:80%
Oh, I gave them to Genius as a gift.

00:07:16.487 --> 00:07:19.865 line:80%
If he presses the buttons,
we can communicate.

00:07:19.948 --> 00:07:22.159 line:80%
I have soccer class,
so I'll be back later.

00:07:22.242 --> 00:07:24.286 line:80%
-Bye.
-Bye.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.454 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:07:25.537 --> 00:07:27.081 line:80%
-Bye.
-[everyone] Bye, Donggu.

00:07:27.164 --> 00:07:28.165 line:80%
[Chan] Bye.

00:07:28.248 --> 00:07:30.292 line:80%
-See you later.
-Ms. Song, sit down.

00:07:30.376 --> 00:07:31.460 line:80%
Right.

00:07:31.543 --> 00:07:34.755 line:80%
We'll need some wine for a welcome party.

00:07:34.838 --> 00:07:36.674 line:80%
Roomie, please get the wine glasses.

00:07:36.757 --> 00:07:37.966 line:80%
-Sure.
-[all cheering]

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:41.637 line:80%
-Mom, I'm going home late today!
-[laughter]

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:44.848 line:80%
[Sol] Raemee, you live with your mother?
Not alone?

00:07:45.683 --> 00:07:47.351 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[laughter]

00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:49.436 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:07:57.361 --> 00:07:59.279 line:80%
[metallic clink echoing]

00:07:59.822 --> 00:08:00.948 line:80%
Can I help with anything?

00:08:02.408 --> 00:08:03.867 line:80%
What? Oh…

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.454 line:80%
Ah. It's okay. Sit down.

00:08:10.165 --> 00:08:11.959 line:80%
[♪ foreboding music plays]

00:08:18.007 --> 00:08:19.216 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:08:21.677 --> 00:08:23.137 line:80%
Please let us clean up.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.346 line:80%
Please.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:26.390 line:80%
The host should clean up.

00:08:26.473 --> 00:08:28.934 line:80%
-Just come have some coffee next time.
-[Sol groans]

00:08:29.018 --> 00:08:30.102 line:80%
-[Hayeong] Okay.
-[Pureum] All right.

00:08:30.185 --> 00:08:32.354 line:80%
-[Sol] Then, we'll come have coffee.
-[Manjae] Okay, thank you.

00:08:32.438 --> 00:08:34.648 line:80%
[everyone] Thank you.

00:08:34.732 --> 00:08:38.527 line:80%
Still, shouldn't at least one of us
stay back and help clean up?

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.738 line:80%
We're going for another round,

00:08:40.821 --> 00:08:43.532 line:80%
so you can help out here, Lightweight.

00:08:43.615 --> 00:08:44.992 line:80%
-Me?
-Yes, you. Song Haran.

00:08:45.075 --> 00:08:46.410 line:80%
-The lightweight.
-Ah.

00:08:46.493 --> 00:08:47.870 line:80%
Then I'll stay and help too…

00:08:47.953 --> 00:08:49.872 line:80%
Come on. You'll just break the cups.

00:08:49.955 --> 00:08:51.540 line:80%
We'll come back next time. Bye.

00:08:51.623 --> 00:08:53.125 line:80%
-See you next time.
-Okay, bye.

00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:54.877 line:80%
-[Sol] I should--
-[Raemee] Let's go.

00:08:55.586 --> 00:08:56.837 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:58.714 line:80%
My gosh.

00:08:58.797 --> 00:08:59.798 line:80%
[whines]

00:09:00.841 --> 00:09:04.053 line:80%
[inhales sharply] I didn't expect them
to all swarm in here.

00:09:04.553 --> 00:09:05.554 line:80%
Yeah.

00:09:07.348 --> 00:09:09.475 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:09:09.558 --> 00:09:11.977 line:80%
Sorry. We're going to drink this later.

00:09:12.061 --> 00:09:13.062 line:80%
[Chan chuckles]

00:09:15.022 --> 00:09:18.317 line:80%
But it's suddenly so quiet
with all of them gone.

00:09:19.068 --> 00:09:21.362 line:80%
Right. It was pretty noisy in here.

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:23.113 line:80%
But, Ms. Song--

00:09:23.197 --> 00:09:24.406 line:80%
[toy] <i>I love you.</i>

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:25.491 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:09:27.743 --> 00:09:30.120 line:80%
-[laughing]
-[clears throat]

00:09:30.204 --> 00:09:33.582 line:80%
Genius, you shouldn't just
keep pressing those.

00:09:33.666 --> 00:09:35.542 line:80%
[clears throat] What I meant to say is…

00:09:35.626 --> 00:09:36.627 line:80%
[toy] <i>I love you.</i>

00:09:37.127 --> 00:09:38.754 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music continues]

00:09:40.255 --> 00:09:43.425 line:80%
[chuckles awkwardly]
Has he not been trained yet?

00:09:43.509 --> 00:09:45.427 line:80%
I was trying to say

00:09:45.928 --> 00:09:48.973 line:80%
that I thought you'd be startled
to see everyone here,

00:09:49.056 --> 00:09:51.475 line:80%
so I sent you a message.

00:09:51.558 --> 00:09:54.561 line:80%
-[chuckling awkwardly] Oh. I see.
-[♪ music fades]

00:09:54.645 --> 00:09:57.231 line:80%
[Manjae exclaims] I'm so full.

00:09:57.314 --> 00:09:59.525 line:80%
I'm going to take a walk with Genius.

00:09:59.608 --> 00:10:01.235 line:80%
You can clean up the rest, right?

00:10:01.318 --> 00:10:02.695 line:80%
Sure. Ms. Song and I--

00:10:02.778 --> 00:10:04.738 line:80%
-[toy] <i>I love you.</i>
-[♪ music continues]

00:10:04.822 --> 00:10:06.407 line:80%
[Manjae exclaims] Oops.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:07.700 line:80%
My mistake. [chuckles]

00:10:07.783 --> 00:10:08.867 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:10:08.951 --> 00:10:10.494 line:80%
See you later. Let's go.

00:10:14.164 --> 00:10:15.207 line:80%
[clears throat]

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.876 line:80%
[chuckles] Let's clean this up, then.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:20.963 line:80%
[Haran exclaims, gasps]

00:10:21.046 --> 00:10:22.381 line:80%
You got it on your sleeve.

00:10:22.464 --> 00:10:24.800 line:80%
It'll get stained
if you don't wash it off.

00:10:25.968 --> 00:10:28.095 line:80%
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

00:10:30.848 --> 00:10:31.890 line:80%
-[♪ music stops]
-[stammers]

00:10:33.142 --> 00:10:34.685 line:80%
I'll go get changed.

00:10:36.103 --> 00:10:39.189 line:80%
[chuckles nervously, clears throat]

00:10:40.566 --> 00:10:42.985 line:80%
[groans] Training on the weekend?

00:10:43.068 --> 00:10:44.653 line:80%
I'm wasting my youth.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.906 line:80%
Oh? It's Song Hadam.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.533 line:80%
Oh? It's Cha Yougyum.

00:10:55.622 --> 00:10:56.790 line:80%
Hi.

00:10:56.874 --> 00:10:58.292 line:80%
I'm Kim Seokhyeon from Class 1.

00:10:58.375 --> 00:11:00.294 line:80%
I've been interested in you,

00:11:00.377 --> 00:11:02.796 line:80%
but I don't have to give up
because of Yougyum now.

00:11:03.881 --> 00:11:05.090 line:80%
Can I have your number?

00:11:05.174 --> 00:11:07.092 line:80%
Hey, what is he saying?

00:11:07.676 --> 00:11:09.303 line:80%
Did you two break up?

00:11:09.803 --> 00:11:12.348 line:80%
[Hadam] <i>Cha Yougyum,</i>
<i>are you just going to watch?</i>

00:11:12.431 --> 00:11:15.559 line:80%
<i>If you don't come until I count to three,</i>
<i>I'm giving him my number.</i>

00:11:15.643 --> 00:11:18.354 line:80%
<i>One, two…</i>

00:11:19.104 --> 00:11:21.106 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:11:21.982 --> 00:11:23.525 line:80%
All right. I'll give it to you.

00:11:28.238 --> 00:11:29.448 line:80%
Text me.

00:11:35.913 --> 00:11:37.790 line:80%
-[boys exclaim teasingly]
-[student 1] You got her number.

00:11:37.873 --> 00:11:40.209 line:80%
-[boy 2] What's this?
-[boy 1] What?

00:11:40.292 --> 00:11:43.045 line:80%
-Please call me if you see her.
-[passersby talk indistinctly]

00:11:43.128 --> 00:11:46.340 line:80%
If you ever see my mother,
please give me a call.

00:11:46.423 --> 00:11:47.883 line:80%
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:52.721 line:80%
[Manjae] Kim Nabong.

00:11:53.806 --> 00:11:55.307 line:80%
[Nana] Hey, Manjae.

00:11:56.183 --> 00:11:57.393 line:80%
Park Genius.

00:11:57.476 --> 00:12:00.312 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-[exclaims] Genius, how have you been?

00:12:00.396 --> 00:12:01.897 line:80%
Were you taking a walk?

00:12:01.981 --> 00:12:04.108 line:80%
Yes, this is a good place to work out.

00:12:04.191 --> 00:12:06.527 line:80%
-I walk a few laps every day.
-No way.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.779 line:80%
I walk him every day here, too.

00:12:08.862 --> 00:12:12.449 line:80%
Well, I guess we wouldn't have
recognized each other until now.

00:12:12.533 --> 00:12:13.534 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:12:13.617 --> 00:12:15.953 line:80%
We can be walking buddies from now on.

00:12:16.036 --> 00:12:17.121 line:80%
[barks, whines]

00:12:17.204 --> 00:12:18.288 line:80%
Hey.

00:12:18.372 --> 00:12:19.832 line:80%
I think he needs to poop.

00:12:19.915 --> 00:12:22.042 line:80%
-He has his own poop area over there.
-[Genius barks]

00:12:22.126 --> 00:12:23.585 line:80%
-Gosh.
-Go and let him poop.

00:12:23.669 --> 00:12:25.796 line:80%
-Okay, I'll see you later.
-[laughs]

00:12:25.879 --> 00:12:27.798 line:80%
Hey, Genius! Slow down.

00:12:27.881 --> 00:12:29.550 line:80%
All right. Goodness.

00:12:29.633 --> 00:12:31.552 line:80%
Slow down. Okay.

00:12:35.556 --> 00:12:37.057 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.686 line:80%
[Manjae] <i>What was she doing here?</i>

00:12:40.769 --> 00:12:43.897 line:80%
-Are you sick or anything?
-I was just visiting a friend there.

00:12:50.029 --> 00:12:51.947 line:80%
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

00:12:57.870 --> 00:12:58.871 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:13:02.124 --> 00:13:03.542 line:80%
[Nana] Is that you, Yougyum?

00:13:07.713 --> 00:13:08.797 line:80%
Hello.

00:13:09.923 --> 00:13:11.675 line:80%
Why are you wearing glasses?

00:13:11.759 --> 00:13:13.427 line:80%
-I almost didn't recognize you.
-[sniffles]

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.137 line:80%
My eyes are swollen.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.472 line:80%
How swollen can they be?

00:13:17.139 --> 00:13:20.809 line:80%
[gasps] My goodness.
They really are incredibly puffy.

00:13:20.893 --> 00:13:22.686 line:80%
How did your eyes get like…

00:13:23.937 --> 00:13:25.272 line:80%
-Are you crying?
-[sobbing]

00:13:27.483 --> 00:13:30.027 line:80%
I had a fight with Hadam,

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:32.529 line:80%
and it feels like
my whole world just fell apart.

00:13:34.657 --> 00:13:37.993 line:80%
How do I live from now on, Ms. Kim?

00:13:40.287 --> 00:13:41.288 line:80%
Follow me.

00:13:42.331 --> 00:13:44.249 line:80%
What? Where…

00:13:48.629 --> 00:13:52.049 line:80%
Fighting won't make the world fall apart.
It only exhausts you.

00:13:52.132 --> 00:13:53.175 line:80%
Eat up.

00:13:53.759 --> 00:13:55.302 line:80%
I don't have an appetite.

00:13:55.386 --> 00:13:59.306 line:80%
To me, Hadam is my whole world
and my whole universe… [groans]

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:02.393 line:80%
You're out. Just break up with Hadam.

00:14:02.977 --> 00:14:04.436 line:80%
-What?
-I'm not letting a guy

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:07.231 line:80%
who bawls after one fight
about the world falling apart

00:14:07.314 --> 00:14:08.565 line:80%
date my granddaughter.

00:14:08.649 --> 00:14:10.985 line:80%
How will you survive the big leagues
with that mentality?

00:14:11.068 --> 00:14:12.695 line:80%
You're out.

00:14:13.278 --> 00:14:14.571 line:80%
No…

00:14:15.322 --> 00:14:16.490 line:80%
I'll eat.

00:14:18.325 --> 00:14:19.702 line:80%
[yelps] Too hot!

00:14:20.577 --> 00:14:24.081 line:80%
I'm only weak when it comes to Hadam.
I push myself hard when I'm training.

00:14:24.164 --> 00:14:26.125 line:80%
I'm the ruthless Cha Yougyum.

00:14:29.128 --> 00:14:33.257 line:80%
Right. At your age, you think the world
falls apart with the smallest things.

00:14:34.383 --> 00:14:35.509 line:80%
I did, too.

00:14:37.428 --> 00:14:41.390 line:80%
But once you go through
something really serious,

00:14:41.473 --> 00:14:45.686 line:80%
you'll realize
that the issues you thought were huge

00:14:45.769 --> 00:14:47.938 line:80%
were actually just tiny specks.

00:14:48.022 --> 00:14:52.109 line:80%
And you'll regret not facing
those issues head-on back then.

00:14:52.192 --> 00:14:54.445 line:80%
You'll think, "Why was I such a coward?"

00:14:55.571 --> 00:14:59.116 line:80%
Anyway, there are dozens of more serious
problems waiting for you in life.

00:14:59.199 --> 00:15:00.701 line:80%
So stop being weak.

00:15:01.785 --> 00:15:02.911 line:80%
Okay.

00:15:04.163 --> 00:15:07.499 line:80%
I'm sorry.
I was absorbed in my own issues.

00:15:08.208 --> 00:15:09.668 line:80%
Ah. What about your checkup?

00:15:09.752 --> 00:15:13.088 line:80%
Something came up at work,
so I rescheduled. [chuckles]

00:15:13.172 --> 00:15:15.507 line:80%
I got scolded
for disappearing from the hospital.

00:15:15.591 --> 00:15:17.801 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:15:19.219 --> 00:15:20.429 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:15:22.514 --> 00:15:25.684 line:80%
I learned that abalones contain ta…

00:15:26.518 --> 00:15:27.686 line:80%
Ta…

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:28.854 line:80%
Taurine.

00:15:28.937 --> 00:15:31.690 line:80%
They contain taurine,
which helps with cognitive function.

00:15:33.776 --> 00:15:36.195 line:80%
All right. Give me all the abalones.

00:15:37.363 --> 00:15:39.948 line:80%
I still have a lot to do,
so I have to stay strong.

00:15:40.032 --> 00:15:43.410 line:80%
You eat up, too.
You need the energy to make up with Hadam.

00:15:43.494 --> 00:15:44.912 line:80%
Right. Energy.

00:15:44.995 --> 00:15:46.747 line:80%
[chuckling]

00:15:47.581 --> 00:15:49.792 line:80%
[slurps] Gosh, that's hot.
[inhales sharply]

00:15:49.875 --> 00:15:52.252 line:80%
[both laughing]

00:15:52.336 --> 00:15:53.337 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:15:57.091 --> 00:15:58.676 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrating]

00:16:01.428 --> 00:16:03.138 line:80%
[cell phone continues vibrating]

00:16:04.723 --> 00:16:06.225 line:80%
Mr. Seonu.

00:16:06.308 --> 00:16:08.310 line:80%
[cell phone continues vibrating]

00:16:09.561 --> 00:16:12.439 line:80%
Mr. Seonu, there's someone calling you.

00:16:16.235 --> 00:16:19.363 line:80%
[knocks on door] Someone keeps calling…

00:16:20.572 --> 00:16:21.740 line:80%
Is he not here?

00:16:23.575 --> 00:16:25.244 line:80%
-[Haran squeals] I'm sorry.
-[Chan exclaims]

00:16:26.078 --> 00:16:27.121 line:80%
Right.

00:16:27.871 --> 00:16:30.040 line:80%
[stutters] What is it?

00:16:30.124 --> 00:16:31.333 line:80%
I…

00:16:31.417 --> 00:16:32.793 line:80%
[hesitates]

00:16:32.876 --> 00:16:35.671 line:80%
Someone kept calling,
so it seemed important.

00:16:36.422 --> 00:16:38.674 line:80%
-I'm sorry.
-Wait.

00:16:38.757 --> 00:16:40.217 line:80%
Yes?

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:41.301 line:80%
I mean…

00:16:44.263 --> 00:16:45.723 line:80%
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

00:16:51.437 --> 00:16:55.024 line:80%
[stutters] We shouldn't do it here…

00:16:55.607 --> 00:16:56.859 line:80%
-I mean…
-No, I…

00:17:00.904 --> 00:17:03.282 line:80%
-Why are you turning off the lights?
-You…

00:17:10.622 --> 00:17:11.623 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:17:11.707 --> 00:17:13.584 line:80%
You're the one who turned them off.

00:17:16.211 --> 00:17:17.421 line:80%
With your back.

00:17:19.965 --> 00:17:22.217 line:80%
Oh. My back… [chuckles awkwardly]

00:17:22.301 --> 00:17:23.761 line:80%
You've got something on your lips.

00:17:23.844 --> 00:17:26.430 line:80%
-[exclaims softly]
-Crumbs or something.

00:17:26.513 --> 00:17:28.766 line:80%
[groans] It was the crackers…

00:17:29.433 --> 00:17:30.768 line:80%
-[Haran clears throat]
-[inhales sharply]

00:17:30.851 --> 00:17:33.020 line:80%
But why did you close your eyes?

00:17:33.103 --> 00:17:34.104 line:80%
[clears throat]

00:17:35.939 --> 00:17:39.526 line:80%
[stutters] Honestly, anyone would have
misunderstood that situation.

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:42.988 line:80%
You held my hand and hugged me yesterday,
so I thought…

00:17:43.072 --> 00:17:44.198 line:80%
You thought what?

00:17:45.282 --> 00:17:48.744 line:80%
I just thought you were moving fast
since you're from the States.

00:17:49.244 --> 00:17:51.121 line:80%
[groans] This is getting weird.

00:17:51.622 --> 00:17:53.248 line:80%
-Stop teasing me.
-[Chan exclaims]

00:17:53.332 --> 00:17:54.541 line:80%
I wasn't teasing you.

00:17:54.625 --> 00:17:56.960 line:80%
I just thought I saw the old you.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.921 line:80%
It was cute. [chuckles]

00:17:59.004 --> 00:18:00.381 line:80%
My old self?

00:18:00.464 --> 00:18:02.299 line:80%
What do you mean?

00:18:05.052 --> 00:18:07.388 line:80%
I think I heard you used to be
much more cheerful.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:09.181 line:80%
From who?

00:18:10.099 --> 00:18:11.350 line:80%
Was it Hayeong?

00:18:12.142 --> 00:18:15.270 line:80%
[stutters] Anyway,
I really wasn't teasing you.

00:18:15.771 --> 00:18:17.690 line:80%
[chuckles softly] I'm sorry.

00:18:18.816 --> 00:18:19.858 line:80%
[sighs]

00:18:19.942 --> 00:18:22.611 line:80%
Ah. I forgot to give you this.

00:18:23.779 --> 00:18:24.947 line:80%
[in English] A welcome drink.

00:18:26.657 --> 00:18:28.951 line:80%
[in Korean] I almost took back my word
about being nice to you.

00:18:31.495 --> 00:18:33.038 line:80%
Can we do it now?

00:18:33.789 --> 00:18:34.790 line:80%
Do what?

00:18:35.708 --> 00:18:37.501 line:80%
[stutters] I meant…

00:18:37.584 --> 00:18:39.420 line:80%
The photos.

00:18:39.503 --> 00:18:40.796 line:80%
Let's check your homework.

00:18:42.172 --> 00:18:43.173 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:18:44.425 --> 00:18:46.427 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:18:49.763 --> 00:18:50.973 line:80%
[Chan hums in approval]

00:18:51.557 --> 00:18:54.351 line:80%
[inhales sharply]
You have a talent for this. [chuckles]

00:18:54.977 --> 00:18:57.104 line:80%
Oh, my gosh.

00:18:58.188 --> 00:18:59.857 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-[sighs]

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:02.192 line:80%
You liar.
You said there were just 10 shots.

00:19:04.695 --> 00:19:08.032 line:80%
Hmm? My Destinations List…

00:19:08.115 --> 00:19:10.868 line:80%
It's yours. I took a photo of it.

00:19:11.869 --> 00:19:14.371 line:80%
-When did you take this?
-What?

00:19:14.913 --> 00:19:16.040 line:80%
This!

00:19:16.123 --> 00:19:20.544 line:80%
[stutters] I just took this for fun
when I was bored…

00:19:20.627 --> 00:19:22.629 line:80%
Wow. That's not fair.

00:19:23.297 --> 00:19:24.840 line:80%
You promised to do that with me.

00:19:25.841 --> 00:19:27.509 line:80%
That doesn't count. I'm confiscating this.

00:19:27.593 --> 00:19:29.345 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-Everything you did alone is invalid.

00:19:29.428 --> 00:19:31.388 line:80%
We'll do everything together.

00:19:31.472 --> 00:19:33.390 line:80%
[scoffs] Geez.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:38.479 line:80%
But what's that last thing
you scribbled out?

00:19:38.562 --> 00:19:41.440 line:80%
[Chan] Mmm. [inhales sharply]

00:19:42.107 --> 00:19:45.569 line:80%
I thought it would be impossible,
so I scribbled it out…

00:19:49.698 --> 00:19:51.033 line:80%
but it might be possible now.

00:19:52.618 --> 00:19:53.952 line:80%
It's a secret, though.

00:19:57.456 --> 00:19:59.917 line:80%
Why did you tell me
to wear comfy shoes today?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.295 line:80%
I thought we'd just walk around a bit

00:20:03.379 --> 00:20:05.172 line:80%
without any specific plans.

00:20:05.255 --> 00:20:07.007 line:80%
Just go wherever the wind takes us?

00:20:07.091 --> 00:20:08.092 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:20:08.467 --> 00:20:10.678 line:80%
I wanted to try that with you.

00:20:11.303 --> 00:20:12.763 line:80%
Go somewhere and try things

00:20:12.846 --> 00:20:16.141 line:80%
without thinking of what happens next.

00:20:17.309 --> 00:20:18.352 line:80%
No,

00:20:19.311 --> 00:20:21.438 line:80%
that may have messed things up.

00:20:22.231 --> 00:20:25.901 line:80%
If things get messed up, we can fix them.
It's the same for knots.

00:20:26.735 --> 00:20:29.613 line:80%
Sometimes they seem impossible to undo,

00:20:30.114 --> 00:20:33.409 line:80%
but if you loosen one strand at a time,
they'll unravel. [chuckles softly]

00:20:34.743 --> 00:20:37.663 line:80%
You can find a way,
no matter how impossible it seems.

00:20:40.749 --> 00:20:42.251 line:80%
Shall we do it tomorrow?

00:20:43.002 --> 00:20:45.796 line:80%
Try going wherever the wind takes us.

00:20:46.588 --> 00:20:48.007 line:80%
-Sorry. Next time.
-[♪ music fades]

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:51.176 line:80%
I have to go somewhere far
with my family tomorrow.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.720 line:80%
Far? Where?

00:20:56.265 --> 00:20:57.266 line:80%
Ah.

00:20:58.183 --> 00:20:59.518 line:80%
THE LATE SONG JUNHO
THE LATE MIN HYEWON

00:20:59.601 --> 00:21:02.896 line:80%
[Hayeong] Dad's favorite crab stew.

00:21:04.231 --> 00:21:05.232 line:80%
[grunts]

00:21:05.316 --> 00:21:08.527 line:80%
Remember when Dad chipped his tooth
eating crab stew?

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:11.530 line:80%
Right, he visited the dentist
for a long time after that. [laughs]

00:21:12.906 --> 00:21:14.491 line:80%
Hadam, wait.

00:21:14.575 --> 00:21:17.286 line:80%
Put the castella on Mom's favorite dish.

00:21:18.078 --> 00:21:21.665 line:80%
[Hayeong] Wow. That's a real antique.
We've had that since I was a baby.

00:21:21.749 --> 00:21:24.543 line:80%
Whenever we were in a bad mood,
she gave us snacks on this.

00:21:24.626 --> 00:21:26.295 line:80%
Mom always said,

00:21:26.378 --> 00:21:30.257 line:80%
"When you're feeling down,
having sweets on a pretty dish

00:21:30.341 --> 00:21:32.509 line:80%
-will make you feel sparkly."
-Sparkly.

00:21:32.593 --> 00:21:34.678 line:80%
[Hayeong, Haran, and Nana laugh]

00:21:35.846 --> 00:21:37.848 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:41.518 line:80%
-[Nana] Let's greet them now.
-[Hayeong] Okay.

00:21:46.148 --> 00:21:49.860 line:80%
[Nana] <i>This might be</i>
<i>my last time coming here.</i>

00:21:51.487 --> 00:21:52.696 line:80%
<i>If, by any chance,</i>

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:56.075 line:80%
<i>I start acting too strange,</i>
<i>just call me home to you quickly.</i>

00:21:56.659 --> 00:21:59.662 line:80%
<i>I don't want to embarrass myself</i>
<i>in front of them.</i>

00:22:00.329 --> 00:22:01.455 line:80%
<i>Okay, Hyewon?</i>

00:22:02.373 --> 00:22:03.582 line:80%
<i>Okay, Junho?</i>

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:14.510 line:80%
I will take you all home safely.

00:22:14.593 --> 00:22:15.803 line:80%
-Let's go.
-[♪ music fades]

00:22:16.512 --> 00:22:17.513 line:80%
[tires screech]

00:22:18.597 --> 00:22:23.435 line:80%
[singsongs] Ah…
My bad feelings are never wrong.

00:22:23.519 --> 00:22:24.520 line:80%
I forgot my phone.

00:22:26.063 --> 00:22:28.357 line:80%
-I'm riding with Haran.
-Eh?

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:31.151 line:80%
You're really going to betray me? Hey!

00:22:32.569 --> 00:22:33.612 line:80%
[Hayeong scoffs]

00:22:33.696 --> 00:22:35.447 line:80%
She's so cold.

00:22:36.657 --> 00:22:39.201 line:80%
[sings in English in tune of Für Elise]
<i>♪ I dream a little bit of red alone ♪</i>

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:47.418 line:80%
[Hayeong in Korean] No, I had it then.

00:22:47.501 --> 00:22:48.711 line:80%
And then, Grandma…

00:22:48.794 --> 00:22:52.089 line:80%
I greeted Mom and Dad,
then I got up, and my phone…

00:22:52.548 --> 00:22:54.049 line:80%
[sighs exasperatedly]
Where did I leave it?

00:22:55.551 --> 00:22:56.635 line:80%
-[man] I'm really sorry.
-Eh?

00:22:56.719 --> 00:22:57.720 line:80%
Who's that?

00:22:57.803 --> 00:22:58.971 line:80%
[man] I'm sorry.

00:22:59.054 --> 00:23:01.640 line:80%
Excuse me, that's my parents' grave.

00:23:01.724 --> 00:23:03.517 line:80%
I think you came to the wrong…

00:23:05.561 --> 00:23:06.770 line:80%
Mr. Yeon?

00:23:07.396 --> 00:23:08.689 line:80%
Why are you…

00:23:09.815 --> 00:23:10.816 line:80%
Are you crying?

00:23:10.899 --> 00:23:12.943 line:80%
Oh… No.

00:23:13.027 --> 00:23:15.446 line:80%
You are. Your eyes are red.

00:23:15.988 --> 00:23:18.073 line:80%
[scoffs] People would think
you're their son…

00:23:20.159 --> 00:23:22.286 line:80%
[♪ emotional music playing]

00:23:22.369 --> 00:23:23.495 line:80%
Thank you.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:26.123 line:80%
[Hyewon] How pretty.

00:23:26.206 --> 00:23:28.834 line:80%
You don't need to do this
for Parents' Day.

00:23:28.917 --> 00:23:32.046 line:80%
You always welcome me
and pack me side dishes.

00:23:32.129 --> 00:23:35.049 line:80%
I'm a bit awkward
with expressing my feelings,

00:23:35.132 --> 00:23:37.509 line:80%
but I really wanted to thank you today.

00:23:37.593 --> 00:23:39.011 line:80%
[exclaims softly]

00:23:39.094 --> 00:23:40.596 line:80%
Goodness. Thank you.

00:23:40.679 --> 00:23:42.514 line:80%
My friends brag about their sons.

00:23:42.598 --> 00:23:45.309 line:80%
I can brag to them that I got
carnations from my son, too.

00:23:45.392 --> 00:23:46.435 line:80%
[all chuckle]

00:23:46.518 --> 00:23:49.980 line:80%
Since we're all dressed up,
how about a family photo?

00:23:50.064 --> 00:23:51.523 line:80%
That sounds great.

00:23:51.607 --> 00:23:53.400 line:80%
-Let's take a photo over there.
-Okay.

00:23:53.484 --> 00:23:56.403 line:80%
-Oh, sure.
-[Junho] Let's take a photo.

00:23:56.487 --> 00:23:58.405 line:80%
-All right.
-[Hyewon] Mr. Yeon.

00:23:58.489 --> 00:24:00.699 line:80%
-Let's take it together.
-Come on, Mr. Yeon.

00:24:00.783 --> 00:24:02.326 line:80%
-Join us.
-Come here.

00:24:02.409 --> 00:24:03.827 line:80%
It's okay.

00:24:03.911 --> 00:24:05.829 line:80%
It's a family photo. Come here.

00:24:05.913 --> 00:24:08.749 line:80%
Sir, can you take a photo of us?

00:24:10.292 --> 00:24:11.418 line:80%
[man] All right.

00:24:11.502 --> 00:24:13.003 line:80%
One, two, three.

00:24:13.087 --> 00:24:14.088 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:24:23.055 --> 00:24:24.515 line:80%
[sighs] Mom, Dad.

00:24:24.598 --> 00:24:27.518 line:80%
Our former chauffeur, Mr. Yeon,
became our COO.

00:24:27.601 --> 00:24:31.730 line:80%
He's a core figure now,
like me in our household.

00:24:32.314 --> 00:24:34.858 line:80%
So send him lots of energy.

00:24:38.779 --> 00:24:40.489 line:80%
Thank you for taking care

00:24:41.740 --> 00:24:43.283 line:80%
of our parents, too.

00:24:46.245 --> 00:24:47.246 line:80%
-I'm sorry.
-[♪ music ends]

00:24:47.705 --> 00:24:50.332 line:80%
Why do you keep saying sorry?

00:24:50.416 --> 00:24:51.417 line:80%
I…

00:24:53.210 --> 00:24:54.837 line:80%
I'm really sorry.

00:24:58.382 --> 00:25:01.468 line:80%
Oh. I dropped my phone somewhere.

00:25:01.552 --> 00:25:03.012 line:80%
Can you call my number?

00:25:06.640 --> 00:25:08.726 line:80%
-[sniffs] Where is it?
-[cell phone ringing]

00:25:08.809 --> 00:25:10.728 line:80%
I hear it. Where is it?

00:25:11.937 --> 00:25:13.772 line:80%
Is it here? Is it here?

00:25:14.356 --> 00:25:15.357 line:80%
Is it here?

00:25:15.441 --> 00:25:16.442 line:80%
[Yeon] I…

00:25:17.609 --> 00:25:19.111 line:80%
It's coming from your butt.

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:21.655 line:80%
-My butt?
-[ringing stops]

00:25:22.281 --> 00:25:25.826 line:80%
Darn it. I came all the way
back up here for nothing.

00:25:26.577 --> 00:25:29.580 line:80%
[sighs heavily] Since we met here,

00:25:30.372 --> 00:25:31.623 line:80%
should we go eat something?

00:25:32.041 --> 00:25:33.042 line:80%
Eat?

00:25:33.125 --> 00:25:35.294 line:80%
I promised you I'd treat you last time.

00:25:35.377 --> 00:25:38.922 line:80%
It was 39,000 won last time,

00:25:40.507 --> 00:25:43.218 line:80%
so I'll treat you to up to 80,000 won.

00:25:43.302 --> 00:25:46.263 line:80%
[gasps] There's an amazing
oxtail soup place nearby.

00:25:46.347 --> 00:25:47.348 line:80%
What do you say?

00:25:47.431 --> 00:25:48.599 line:80%
Let's go!

00:25:48.682 --> 00:25:50.559 line:80%
[Yeon hesitates] It's okay…

00:25:50.643 --> 00:25:52.186 line:80%
No, it's not okay.

00:25:52.811 --> 00:25:54.647 line:80%
Have we eaten together before?

00:25:54.730 --> 00:25:56.774 line:80%
Who do you normally
have lunch with at work?

00:25:56.857 --> 00:25:59.401 line:80%
What do you usually do on the weekend?

00:25:59.485 --> 00:26:00.569 line:80%
[Yeon] Wait.

00:26:00.653 --> 00:26:02.363 line:80%
[♪ light-hearted music playing]

00:26:04.948 --> 00:26:05.949 line:80%
Your hand.

00:26:06.033 --> 00:26:08.160 line:80%
[Yeon] You might slip
since you're wearing heels.

00:26:12.289 --> 00:26:13.749 line:80%
It's fine, I can wipe them.

00:26:14.416 --> 00:26:15.417 line:80%
Be careful.

00:26:18.462 --> 00:26:20.464 line:80%
[♪ light-hearted music continues]

00:26:22.675 --> 00:26:23.926 line:80%
[stammers]

00:26:24.009 --> 00:26:26.345 line:80%
You really are considerate.

00:26:27.054 --> 00:26:29.306 line:80%
You always look out for our family.

00:26:32.768 --> 00:26:34.728 line:80%
<i>Why did he cry, though?</i>

00:26:36.438 --> 00:26:37.439 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:26:40.442 --> 00:26:41.443 line:80%
[cell phone vibrates]

00:26:42.152 --> 00:26:43.779 line:80%
[Chan] <i>How was your visit to your parents?</i>

00:26:44.279 --> 00:26:45.531 line:80%
[Hayeong] Hey.

00:26:45.614 --> 00:26:48.033 line:80%
Whose message
is making you smile like that?

00:26:48.659 --> 00:26:49.952 line:80%
What?

00:26:50.035 --> 00:26:52.746 line:80%
What took you so long?
Weren't you looking for your phone?

00:26:52.830 --> 00:26:54.748 line:80%
I was hungry, so I got some oxtail soup.

00:26:55.374 --> 00:26:56.917 line:80%
[grunts] I'm so full.

00:26:57.001 --> 00:26:58.293 line:80%
[chuckling] That's good.

00:26:58.377 --> 00:26:59.753 line:80%
Hey, Hayeong.

00:27:00.546 --> 00:27:04.717 line:80%
Did you ever tell Mr. Seonu about my past?

00:27:04.800 --> 00:27:07.761 line:80%
Like how I was different before
or something like that?

00:27:07.845 --> 00:27:11.265 line:80%
Like how you used to be
really bubbly and friendly?

00:27:11.348 --> 00:27:12.725 line:80%
Something like that.

00:27:12.808 --> 00:27:14.351 line:80%
Mmm? No, I didn't…

00:27:15.811 --> 00:27:17.688 line:80%
[gasps] Wait, did I?

00:27:18.522 --> 00:27:20.774 line:80%
[groans] I'm 29 now.

00:27:20.858 --> 00:27:22.067 line:80%
My memory isn't so good…

00:27:23.402 --> 00:27:26.655 line:80%
-But why do you ask?
-He spoke as if he knew me.

00:27:27.114 --> 00:27:28.115 line:80%
Really?

00:27:29.283 --> 00:27:32.328 line:80%
But are you two really close?

00:27:32.411 --> 00:27:34.538 line:80%
Mr. Seonu, Ms. Song…

00:27:34.621 --> 00:27:35.748 line:80%
You're so formal.

00:27:36.582 --> 00:27:38.542 line:80%
Then what should I call him?

00:27:38.625 --> 00:27:40.210 line:80%
You're the same age.

00:27:40.294 --> 00:27:41.920 line:80%
Use your first names.

00:27:42.004 --> 00:27:44.673 line:80%
You can just say, "Hey, Haran. Hey, Chan…"

00:27:47.259 --> 00:27:48.427 line:80%
I should go shower.

00:27:48.510 --> 00:27:49.887 line:80%
Why did you suddenly stop?

00:27:50.721 --> 00:27:51.805 line:80%
Well…

00:27:52.931 --> 00:27:55.142 line:80%
You used to call him Chan.

00:27:55.934 --> 00:27:59.229 line:80%
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

00:28:00.522 --> 00:28:02.691 line:80%
I just realized their names were similar.

00:28:03.567 --> 00:28:04.943 line:80%
Oh…

00:28:05.027 --> 00:28:07.571 line:80%
Right. I didn't think about that.

00:28:07.655 --> 00:28:09.698 line:80%
[♪ emotional music playing]

00:28:09.782 --> 00:28:11.158 line:80%
[mumbles]

00:28:12.159 --> 00:28:13.869 line:80%
[mumbling] Make…

00:28:13.952 --> 00:28:17.581 line:80%
MAKE HER HAPPY AGAIN, NO MATTER WHAT!

00:28:18.165 --> 00:28:19.166 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:28:19.583 --> 00:28:22.252 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Their names… were similar.</i>

00:28:23.045 --> 00:28:24.296 line:80%
[sighs] All right…

00:28:26.799 --> 00:28:28.759 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:28:28.842 --> 00:28:29.843 line:80%
[sighs]

00:28:30.427 --> 00:28:32.513 line:80%
-[thuds loudly]
-[metallic clink echoes]

00:28:33.639 --> 00:28:35.099 line:80%
What was that?

00:28:35.599 --> 00:28:38.477 line:80%
EMPTY SPOT IN MEMORY - FOURTH

00:28:39.645 --> 00:28:41.814 line:80%
<i>A waste container…</i>

00:28:42.690 --> 00:28:43.774 line:80%
<i>and that sound again.</i>

00:28:45.818 --> 00:28:47.236 line:80%
<i>The lab…</i>

00:28:47.319 --> 00:28:48.821 line:80%
<i>The sound of metal…</i>

00:28:48.904 --> 00:28:50.155 line:80%
<i>The explosion.</i>

00:28:50.239 --> 00:28:53.909 line:80%
<i>The missing gap</i>
<i>started with that sound, too.</i>

00:28:57.579 --> 00:28:59.415 line:80%
<i>And the second memory</i>

00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:01.250 line:80%
<i>had that sound as well.</i>

00:29:02.751 --> 00:29:04.545 line:80%
-[Sujin exclaims]
-[metallic clink]

00:29:04.628 --> 00:29:08.590 line:80%
[Chan] <i>And the third memory</i>
<i>had the same sound.</i>

00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:11.885 line:80%
<i>Why did those missing memories</i>

00:29:12.678 --> 00:29:14.847 line:80%
<i>start with the sound of her bracelet?</i>

00:29:14.930 --> 00:29:16.849 line:80%
[Hyeokchan] <i>Sorry, Ran.</i>
<i>My professor's calling.</i>

00:29:16.932 --> 00:29:18.017 line:80%
<i>I'll call you back later.</i>

00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:19.435 line:80%
Hey, Sujin. You're here?

00:29:19.935 --> 00:29:23.605 line:80%
Why are they all connected to this person?

00:29:27.276 --> 00:29:30.070 line:20%
SUJIN?

00:29:30.988 --> 00:29:32.531 line:80%
Sujin?

00:29:34.825 --> 00:29:36.410 line:80%
[metallic clink echoes]

00:29:40.497 --> 00:29:42.499 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

00:29:49.465 --> 00:29:51.050 line:80%
This is Cha Sujin.

00:29:51.133 --> 00:29:52.718 line:80%
I've arrived in Korea.

00:29:52.801 --> 00:29:54.803 line:80%
I'll head to the hospital straight away.

00:29:55.554 --> 00:29:57.640 line:80%
[metallic clink echoes]

00:30:00.100 --> 00:30:01.101 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:30:01.602 --> 00:30:03.854 line:80%
It's my fault for causing
the misunderstanding.

00:30:04.563 --> 00:30:05.731 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:30:07.149 --> 00:30:08.567 line:80%
I'm sorry about everything.

00:30:09.485 --> 00:30:10.736 line:80%
[taps]

00:30:14.073 --> 00:30:15.574 line:80%
I'm sorry about everything.

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:17.576 line:80%
I'm sorry about everything…

00:30:23.832 --> 00:30:26.126 line:80%
[Hadam] <i>I'll give it to you. Text me.</i>

00:30:26.627 --> 00:30:28.629 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:30:33.509 --> 00:30:36.011 line:80%
[groaning]

00:30:49.858 --> 00:30:50.859 line:80%
[Changmo] Cha Yougyum?

00:30:52.778 --> 00:30:54.863 line:80%
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:30:54.947 --> 00:30:55.948 line:80%
[breathing shakily]

00:30:56.031 --> 00:30:58.659 line:20%
[Yougyum singing heartbreaking ballad]

00:31:08.335 --> 00:31:10.337 line:80%
[crying]

00:31:14.550 --> 00:31:16.301 line:80%
What are you doing? Give it.

00:31:17.594 --> 00:31:19.596 line:80%
[continues singing]

00:31:26.353 --> 00:31:29.398 line:80%
[shatter echoes]

00:31:31.150 --> 00:31:32.359 line:80%
[Hayeong] Are you okay?

00:31:33.193 --> 00:31:34.486 line:80%
Oh?

00:31:34.570 --> 00:31:35.571 line:80%
That's Mom's dish.

00:31:35.654 --> 00:31:37.156 line:80%
Song Hadam.

00:31:37.239 --> 00:31:38.741 line:80%
Don't you know we never use that?

00:31:38.824 --> 00:31:40.617 line:80%
There are dozens of dishes. Why did you--

00:31:40.701 --> 00:31:43.120 line:80%
Then why are you making a fuss
over one dish?

00:31:43.203 --> 00:31:45.706 line:80%
Hey. Why are you talking like that?

00:31:45.789 --> 00:31:47.666 line:80%
Don't you know what that dish is?

00:31:47.750 --> 00:31:48.959 line:80%
-It's Mom's--
-I don't!

00:31:49.710 --> 00:31:50.753 line:80%
I don't know.

00:31:50.836 --> 00:31:52.546 line:80%
I'm the only one who doesn't know.

00:31:52.629 --> 00:31:55.257 line:80%
I can hardly even remember
Mom and Dad's voices or faces,

00:31:55.341 --> 00:31:58.093 line:80%
so how would I know
how special that stupid dish is?

00:31:58.177 --> 00:32:00.346 line:80%
I want to remember, too.

00:32:00.429 --> 00:32:02.389 line:80%
I want to miss them too,

00:32:03.057 --> 00:32:05.142 line:80%
but I can't remember.

00:32:07.186 --> 00:32:11.982 line:80%
Whenever you talk about Mom and Dad,
I feel like I don't belong.

00:32:12.816 --> 00:32:15.569 line:80%
I feel like I'm the only one
who wasn't their daughter.

00:32:17.071 --> 00:32:19.698 line:80%
-Hey…
-I was only six.

00:32:20.324 --> 00:32:21.533 line:80%
I…

00:32:22.826 --> 00:32:24.286 line:80%
I didn't know anything…

00:32:24.370 --> 00:32:25.871 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:32:25.954 --> 00:32:26.955 line:80%
Hadam.

00:32:27.665 --> 00:32:28.707 line:80%
We're sorry.

00:32:28.791 --> 00:32:30.376 line:80%
[crying] I'm sorry, Hadam.

00:32:31.293 --> 00:32:33.295 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:32:35.422 --> 00:32:36.632 line:80%
[Hadam] I'm going to school.

00:32:37.549 --> 00:32:38.926 line:80%
I'm really sorry…

00:32:41.595 --> 00:32:42.805 line:80%
I broke Mom's dish.

00:32:48.310 --> 00:32:49.478 line:80%
[sighs]

00:32:50.562 --> 00:32:51.563 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:32:53.023 --> 00:32:54.024 line:80%
[sighs]

00:32:54.608 --> 00:32:58.028 line:80%
You said you have a meeting.
Go get ready. I'll clean this.

00:32:58.570 --> 00:32:59.738 line:80%
[sighs]

00:33:00.531 --> 00:33:01.615 line:80%
Okay, thanks.

00:33:02.241 --> 00:33:04.243 line:80%
We'll talk to Hadam when she comes home.

00:33:05.244 --> 00:33:07.079 line:80%
[dish clinking]

00:33:16.046 --> 00:33:17.172 line:80%
Hey, Hadam.

00:33:20.342 --> 00:33:22.386 line:80%
Let me see your hand. Where is it?

00:33:23.387 --> 00:33:24.638 line:80%
[sighs] Gosh.

00:33:26.307 --> 00:33:27.308 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:33:30.769 --> 00:33:32.896 line:80%
I just got this at a convenience store.

00:33:32.980 --> 00:33:34.273 line:80%
It's just a temporary fix,

00:33:34.356 --> 00:33:37.693 line:80%
so go to the nurse's office, okay?

00:33:38.819 --> 00:33:41.280 line:80%
But what do we do

00:33:42.281 --> 00:33:43.490 line:80%
about Mom's dish?

00:33:44.074 --> 00:33:45.826 line:80%
That dish isn't the problem.

00:33:45.909 --> 00:33:47.911 line:80%
You hurt your hand
when the CSAT is coming up.

00:33:48.579 --> 00:33:50.205 line:80%
I'm ambidextrous.

00:33:51.457 --> 00:33:53.459 line:80%
You are? Since when?

00:33:53.542 --> 00:33:55.336 line:80%
I practiced using my left hand

00:33:55.419 --> 00:33:57.463 line:80%
because my hand hurt
when I studied too long.

00:33:57.546 --> 00:33:59.089 line:80%
But I was a natural at it.

00:33:59.757 --> 00:34:01.008 line:80%
Our baby sister.

00:34:01.759 --> 00:34:03.052 line:80%
You take after Mom.

00:34:04.678 --> 00:34:05.679 line:80%
Mom?

00:34:06.764 --> 00:34:08.349 line:80%
Mom was ambidextrous.

00:34:09.224 --> 00:34:11.268 line:80%
[exclaims] We wondered
where her genes went.

00:34:11.352 --> 00:34:13.270 line:80%
I guess they all went to you.

00:34:13.771 --> 00:34:15.606 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:34:15.689 --> 00:34:19.693 line:80%
Did you want to find out
what she meant by feeling sparkly?

00:34:20.694 --> 00:34:21.987 line:80%
Is that why you took it out?

00:34:22.613 --> 00:34:23.614 line:80%
Huh?

00:34:23.697 --> 00:34:28.243 line:80%
Didn't you want to eat sweets from it
and feel better?

00:34:32.122 --> 00:34:33.248 line:80%
Hadam.

00:34:33.332 --> 00:34:36.043 line:80%
Let's talk more about Mom and Dad
from now on.

00:34:37.252 --> 00:34:41.840 line:80%
I was actually worried
we'd forget about them when time passed.

00:34:41.924 --> 00:34:45.511 line:80%
But I guess we can tell
our smart baby sister about them

00:34:45.594 --> 00:34:47.012 line:80%
as a backup file.

00:34:48.180 --> 00:34:51.100 line:80%
I do have a good memory.

00:34:51.183 --> 00:34:52.476 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:34:52.559 --> 00:34:55.896 line:80%
How long are you going to follow me?

00:34:57.356 --> 00:35:00.567 line:80%
I'm escorting you properly today,

00:35:01.026 --> 00:35:02.194 line:80%
all the way to school.

00:35:03.320 --> 00:35:07.908 line:80%
Aren't you the least bit aware
of your current condition?

00:35:09.118 --> 00:35:11.620 line:80%
-Are you embarrassed of me?
-A bit.

00:35:12.413 --> 00:35:13.580 line:80%
Hadam!

00:35:13.664 --> 00:35:15.165 line:80%
[Hadam] Oh? It's Yeongju.

00:35:15.249 --> 00:35:16.458 line:80%
Bye.

00:35:16.542 --> 00:35:17.668 line:80%
Jeong Yeongju!

00:35:18.460 --> 00:35:20.129 line:80%
Go to the nurse's office!

00:35:21.213 --> 00:35:23.632 line:80%
You'll catch a cold. Go home.

00:35:24.717 --> 00:35:26.343 line:80%
Bye! [giggles]

00:35:36.353 --> 00:35:37.438 line:80%
[sighs]

00:35:37.521 --> 00:35:38.522 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:35:39.231 --> 00:35:41.650 line:80%
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

00:35:44.153 --> 00:35:46.989 line:80%
[toy] <i>Let's go on a walk.</i>

00:35:47.072 --> 00:35:49.158 line:80%
-[sighs] Genius.
-[toy] <i>Let's go on a walk.</i>

00:35:49.241 --> 00:35:51.118 line:80%
You seem to be abusing that.

00:35:51.201 --> 00:35:55.414 line:80%
-And you're such a chatterbox.
-[whimpers]

00:35:55.497 --> 00:35:56.707 line:80%
Watch your mouth, okay?

00:35:57.082 --> 00:35:58.083 line:80%
[grunts]

00:35:58.167 --> 00:36:00.753 line:80%
-[toy] <i>Let's play.</i>
-Okay. [chuckles]

00:36:01.378 --> 00:36:02.379 line:80%
Let's go on a walk.

00:36:02.463 --> 00:36:04.590 line:80%
Mr. Park, I'll go on a run with Genius.

00:36:04.673 --> 00:36:06.050 line:80%
Don't you have a meeting?

00:36:06.133 --> 00:36:07.468 line:80%
I still have some time.

00:36:07.551 --> 00:36:08.761 line:80%
Right.

00:36:08.844 --> 00:36:12.056 line:80%
Something arrived from the US
while you were away.

00:36:12.139 --> 00:36:14.767 line:80%
I forgot about it.
It's in the counter cabinet.

00:36:14.850 --> 00:36:15.851 line:80%
Ah.

00:36:22.941 --> 00:36:24.943 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:36:27.404 --> 00:36:28.405 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:36:32.743 --> 00:36:33.744 line:80%
Mmm?

00:36:38.332 --> 00:36:39.333 line:80%
Hello?

00:36:40.793 --> 00:36:42.294 line:80%
What was that message?

00:36:42.878 --> 00:36:44.463 line:80%
Why is it a secret from Ms. Song?

00:36:47.132 --> 00:36:48.133 line:80%
Ah.

00:36:48.842 --> 00:36:51.345 line:80%
Okay, I'll keep it a secret. All right.

00:36:53.722 --> 00:36:55.265 line:80%
What did you receive?

00:36:55.349 --> 00:36:58.018 line:80%
[chuckles awkwardly] It's nothing special.

00:36:58.102 --> 00:36:59.311 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

00:37:00.354 --> 00:37:02.523 line:80%
I'll clean up. Go. He's so eager to leave.

00:37:02.606 --> 00:37:03.899 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:37:03.983 --> 00:37:05.818 line:80%
-Genius, let's go. Come on.
-Go on.

00:37:06.694 --> 00:37:08.570 line:80%
[Chan] Let's go, Genius.

00:37:08.654 --> 00:37:09.863 line:80%
-Let's run!
-[chuckles]

00:37:10.614 --> 00:37:11.615 line:80%
[grunts]

00:37:13.409 --> 00:37:14.827 line:80%
[humming]

00:37:14.910 --> 00:37:16.078 line:80%
[exclaims softly]

00:37:20.457 --> 00:37:21.458 line:80%
What is this?

00:37:22.042 --> 00:37:24.962 line:80%
[in English] "Newbury Street, Boston…"

00:37:25.796 --> 00:37:27.423 line:80%
[in Korean] What was the package?

00:37:28.465 --> 00:37:29.800 line:80%
-[patron 1] Hello, Mr. Park.
-Oh!

00:37:29.883 --> 00:37:32.011 line:80%
-[patron 2] Hello.
-Welcome. Come in.

00:37:36.890 --> 00:37:39.560 line:80%
You mean there will be
more parts on Korea?

00:37:39.643 --> 00:37:43.188 line:80%
Yes, the interim feedback
was really positive.

00:37:43.272 --> 00:37:46.025 line:80%
The response to Won's outfit
was incredible.

00:37:46.108 --> 00:37:50.696 line:80%
The cloud motif, Korean color palette,
<i>dancheong, </i>and the hanbok panel.

00:37:50.779 --> 00:37:55.868 line:80%
Wow. Everyone was impressed
by the details that represented Korea.

00:37:55.951 --> 00:38:00.956 line:80%
The most Korean things
are what end up being popular worldwide!

00:38:01.540 --> 00:38:06.086 line:80%
So we'd like to request another outfit
once we get the revised script,

00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:09.089 line:80%
if that's okay with you…

00:38:09.173 --> 00:38:11.842 line:80%
Don't be silly. Of course, that's okay.

00:38:12.634 --> 00:38:15.012 line:80%
If it will help with the project,
anything's fine.

00:38:16.972 --> 00:38:18.390 line:80%
-Thank you.
-[Ben] Thank you.

00:38:18.932 --> 00:38:21.185 line:80%
Right. We just have to push
straight ahead now.

00:38:21.268 --> 00:38:23.312 line:80%
Let's pick up the pace again.

00:38:23.395 --> 00:38:25.147 line:80%
How about a round of applause?

00:38:25.230 --> 00:38:27.650 line:80%
Everybody, clap!

00:38:27.733 --> 00:38:29.485 line:80%
[applause]

00:38:37.326 --> 00:38:39.995 line:80%
Plans? Is it about work?

00:38:40.913 --> 00:38:41.997 line:80%
[Chan] Mmm…

00:38:42.081 --> 00:38:43.916 line:80%
I think it's a secret.

00:38:51.215 --> 00:38:54.051 line:80%
There should at least be
one pen that you like.

00:38:56.136 --> 00:38:58.305 line:80%
I guess she didn't find
any that she liked.

00:38:58.806 --> 00:38:59.807 line:80%
What?

00:38:59.890 --> 00:39:00.933 line:80%
It's nothing. [chuckles softly]

00:39:01.016 --> 00:39:02.226 line:80%
[elevator dings]

00:39:02.309 --> 00:39:03.686 line:80%
Bye, then.

00:39:05.187 --> 00:39:06.313 line:80%
Bye.

00:39:07.898 --> 00:39:09.358 line:80%
See you later. I'll text you.

00:39:14.154 --> 00:39:16.699 line:80%
Who is he meeting, though?

00:39:17.491 --> 00:39:20.327 line:80%
[Nana] Then are your parents
in LA as well?

00:39:20.411 --> 00:39:21.620 line:80%
[♪ traditional Korean music plays]

00:39:21.704 --> 00:39:24.248 line:80%
Oh… No. [inhales sharply]

00:39:24.790 --> 00:39:26.959 line:80%
My mother passed away when I was nine.

00:39:27.042 --> 00:39:31.005 line:80%
My father's probably teaching in Daejeon.

00:39:31.088 --> 00:39:32.631 line:80%
We don't really keep in touch.

00:39:33.674 --> 00:39:34.675 line:80%
Well…

00:39:35.175 --> 00:39:39.471 line:80%
Every family has its own issues.

00:39:40.347 --> 00:39:41.932 line:80%
Go on and eat.

00:39:42.016 --> 00:39:43.392 line:80%
Thank you.

00:39:43.475 --> 00:39:44.643 line:80%
Right.

00:39:44.727 --> 00:39:47.813 line:80%
Will you stay in LA again
once the collaboration is over?

00:39:47.896 --> 00:39:48.981 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:39:49.064 --> 00:39:51.817 line:80%
Yes, I believe so. But why do you ask?

00:39:52.901 --> 00:39:55.362 line:80%
Should I establish a branch in LA
and send her there?

00:39:56.405 --> 00:39:57.573 line:80%
Excuse me?

00:39:57.656 --> 00:40:00.200 line:80%
Ah. I was just talking to myself.

00:40:00.284 --> 00:40:03.912 line:80%
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-But why aren't you eating? Hmm?

00:40:03.996 --> 00:40:07.416 line:80%
I wanted to treat you to something
after all that trouble at headquarters.

00:40:07.499 --> 00:40:08.542 line:80%
Eat up.

00:40:08.625 --> 00:40:12.504 line:80%
Why did you only ask for me?
Ben went through a lot, too.

00:40:12.588 --> 00:40:14.590 line:80%
-Who?
-You know, with the…

00:40:15.174 --> 00:40:18.344 line:80%
Oh… Producer Ben?

00:40:18.427 --> 00:40:19.762 line:80%
Well,

00:40:19.845 --> 00:40:22.931 line:80%
I'm sure his in-laws
will take good care of him.

00:40:23.015 --> 00:40:26.226 line:80%
Just think of this as a meal
from your in-laws.

00:40:26.310 --> 00:40:28.604 line:80%
-[Nana chuckles]
-In-laws?

00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:32.733 line:80%
-I'm just saying…
-[♪ music fades]

00:40:32.816 --> 00:40:34.860 line:80%
[groans] Darn it. I can't do this.

00:40:36.862 --> 00:40:38.072 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:40:38.155 --> 00:40:40.658 line:80%
Beating around the bush
isn't really my style,

00:40:40.741 --> 00:40:42.242 line:80%
so let me be blunt.

00:40:42.326 --> 00:40:44.036 line:80%
Oh. Sure, be blunt…

00:40:44.662 --> 00:40:46.538 line:80%
I mean, feel free to say what you want.

00:40:48.248 --> 00:40:51.293 line:80%
How much do you know about Haran's past?

00:40:52.294 --> 00:40:53.587 line:80%
Quite a lot.

00:40:55.047 --> 00:40:57.508 line:80%
Did you hear about her losing her parents?

00:40:59.051 --> 00:41:00.052 line:80%
I heard.

00:41:00.135 --> 00:41:03.347 line:80%
And losing her boyfriend seven years ago?

00:41:06.767 --> 00:41:08.143 line:80%
I know that, too.

00:41:11.480 --> 00:41:12.856 line:80%
Even after losing her parents,

00:41:13.857 --> 00:41:16.276 line:80%
she stayed strong,

00:41:17.194 --> 00:41:20.364 line:80%
but that incident left Haran
trapped in winter,

00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:23.450 line:80%
just like you said.

00:41:24.118 --> 00:41:25.244 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:41:25.327 --> 00:41:26.787 line:80%
Haran's not eating.

00:41:26.870 --> 00:41:28.205 line:80%
Again?

00:41:28.288 --> 00:41:31.542 line:80%
She's not eating or sleeping.

00:41:31.625 --> 00:41:33.127 line:80%
She'll die at this rate, Grandma.

00:41:34.586 --> 00:41:37.423 line:80%
[Nana] <i>She no longer smiled</i>
<i>or showed any expressions…</i>

00:41:37.506 --> 00:41:40.217 line:80%
-Eat a sausage, Hadam.
<i>-…even in front of her sisters,</i>

00:41:40.300 --> 00:41:42.720 line:80%
<i>and even in front of me,</i>
<i>when we used to be like friends.</i>

00:41:42.803 --> 00:41:44.513 line:80%
[Haran] Just don't go.

00:41:44.596 --> 00:41:46.974 line:80%
What if something happens to you outside?

00:41:47.057 --> 00:41:50.102 line:80%
It happened to Mom and Dad.
So don't go, okay?

00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:54.315 line:80%
It's okay.
Haran, it's all right. It's okay.

00:41:54.398 --> 00:41:56.817 line:80%
<i>If I let her stay buried</i>
<i>in all that anxiety,</i>

00:41:57.401 --> 00:41:59.069 line:80%
<i>I felt like I would lose her.</i>

00:42:03.949 --> 00:42:05.075 line:80%
Come out.

00:42:05.159 --> 00:42:06.160 line:80%
I'm not eating.

00:42:07.244 --> 00:42:08.620 line:80%
Just leave me alone.

00:42:08.704 --> 00:42:10.289 line:80%
Get up. Right now.

00:42:10.372 --> 00:42:14.376 line:80%
<i>I knew I had to do whatever I could</i>
<i>to pull her out.</i>

00:42:15.377 --> 00:42:16.920 line:80%
You're working here from now on.

00:42:17.004 --> 00:42:19.089 line:80%
I'll give you a month
to organize the storage room.

00:42:19.173 --> 00:42:21.258 line:80%
Why are you doing this?

00:42:21.967 --> 00:42:23.969 line:80%
I don't want to. I'm leaving.

00:42:24.595 --> 00:42:25.596 line:80%
That's an order.

00:42:25.679 --> 00:42:28.057 line:80%
If you want to keep sleeping
under my roof,

00:42:28.682 --> 00:42:29.808 line:80%
do as I say.

00:42:30.643 --> 00:42:34.104 line:80%
<i>I had to grow cold,</i>
<i>and I had to stay strong.</i>

00:42:34.188 --> 00:42:37.566 line:80%
<i>I had to save her first.</i>

00:42:38.609 --> 00:42:39.943 line:80%
[door slams]

00:42:40.444 --> 00:42:41.445 line:80%
[sighs]

00:42:47.368 --> 00:42:48.369 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:42:49.870 --> 00:42:51.038 line:80%
[lightbulb buzzing]

00:42:54.166 --> 00:42:55.167 line:80%
[sighs]

00:42:59.463 --> 00:43:01.423 line:80%
-[buttons clatter]
-[sighs]

00:43:01.507 --> 00:43:03.509 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:43:17.064 --> 00:43:18.357 line:80%
Come out.

00:43:23.570 --> 00:43:25.864 line:80%
[Nana] <i>She could hardly move an inch,</i>

00:43:25.948 --> 00:43:29.243 line:80%
<i>but she finally started moving</i>
<i>little by little,</i>

00:43:29.326 --> 00:43:30.995 line:80%
<i>and her eyes started shining.</i>

00:43:33.914 --> 00:43:34.999 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:43:42.256 --> 00:43:45.342 line:80%
[Nana] <i>She was living again,</i>
<i>little by little.</i>

00:43:54.852 --> 00:43:56.395 line:80%
She's alive now.

00:44:00.816 --> 00:44:02.818 line:80%
[♪ uplifting music playing]

00:44:07.406 --> 00:44:09.658 line:80%
Come to work on the third floor
starting tomorrow.

00:44:10.492 --> 00:44:15.205 line:80%
<i>You'll be the rookie assistant</i>
<i>for Design Team 1, 2, and 3.</i>

00:44:17.624 --> 00:44:20.878 line:80%
<i>I was relieved at the fact</i>
<i>that she held on once more</i>

00:44:20.961 --> 00:44:22.755 line:80%
<i>without crumbling down.</i>

00:44:22.838 --> 00:44:25.466 line:80%
<i>But then, she changed.</i>

00:44:25.549 --> 00:44:28.344 line:80%
-This is an apology for taking a leave.
-[Pureum] Thank you.

00:44:28.427 --> 00:44:30.346 line:80%
[Nana] <i>She started smiling again recently.</i>

00:44:31.430 --> 00:44:34.224 line:80%
I know I met a great person.

00:44:34.308 --> 00:44:36.060 line:80%
I feel grateful.

00:44:37.061 --> 00:44:38.687 line:80%
[Nana] <i>She learned how to cry again, too.</i>

00:44:43.442 --> 00:44:44.568 line:80%
Mr. Seonu.

00:44:46.987 --> 00:44:48.238 line:80%
Why would you…

00:44:48.697 --> 00:44:49.698 line:80%
Thank you.

00:44:50.366 --> 00:44:52.534 line:80%
I wanted to speak to you today

00:44:52.618 --> 00:44:55.037 line:80%
as Haran's grandmother,
not the head of the atelier.

00:44:55.996 --> 00:44:59.583 line:80%
Thank you so much for letting me see Haran

00:44:59.667 --> 00:45:02.836 line:80%
crying and laughing again.

00:45:04.296 --> 00:45:06.006 line:80%
[stammers] No, I…

00:45:06.757 --> 00:45:07.841 line:80%
I didn't do anything…

00:45:07.925 --> 00:45:09.677 line:80%
They say that if it's fate,

00:45:09.760 --> 00:45:12.137 line:80%
you'll meet
no matter how far apart you are.

00:45:12.221 --> 00:45:13.555 line:80%
You came all the way here.

00:45:13.639 --> 00:45:15.933 line:80%
I don't think
you were meant to just work here.

00:45:16.016 --> 00:45:17.351 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:45:17.434 --> 00:45:18.477 line:80%
Thanks to you,

00:45:19.395 --> 00:45:20.980 line:80%
I'll be able to leave in peace.

00:45:22.648 --> 00:45:24.108 line:80%
Are you going somewhere?

00:45:25.109 --> 00:45:26.110 line:80%
Well,

00:45:27.528 --> 00:45:31.073 line:80%
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

00:45:31.156 --> 00:45:32.783 line:80%
If you stay by Haran's side,

00:45:32.866 --> 00:45:35.786 line:80%
I won't be that worried about her.

00:45:35.869 --> 00:45:37.579 line:80%
Ah. [sighs]

00:45:39.581 --> 00:45:42.793 line:80%
[inhales sharply] But, Ms. Kim,

00:45:44.044 --> 00:45:46.755 line:80%
I may not be as good for her

00:45:48.257 --> 00:45:51.885 line:80%
as you believe.

00:45:52.428 --> 00:45:54.430 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

00:45:59.518 --> 00:46:02.229 line:80%
My heart is throbbing,

00:46:03.439 --> 00:46:05.149 line:80%
and tears keep flowing.

00:46:05.899 --> 00:46:06.900 line:80%
My heart

00:46:08.068 --> 00:46:09.737 line:80%
hurts more than my foot.

00:46:10.863 --> 00:46:12.573 line:80%
Do you think it's serious?

00:46:12.656 --> 00:46:16.118 line:80%
Cut the drama and go to a bigger hospital.

00:46:16.201 --> 00:46:17.786 line:80%
I can't treat that properly here.

00:46:17.870 --> 00:46:20.414 line:80%
I'm sure it's just because
I trained hard these days.

00:46:20.956 --> 00:46:22.583 line:80%
Just give me something for the bruise.

00:46:22.666 --> 00:46:24.251 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:46:24.335 --> 00:46:25.336 line:80%
[sighs]

00:46:30.257 --> 00:46:31.592 line:80%
Can you move aside?

00:46:31.675 --> 00:46:33.344 line:80%
Huh? Oh…

00:46:33.427 --> 00:46:34.428 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:46:43.604 --> 00:46:44.938 line:80%
Can I help you with anything?

00:46:45.022 --> 00:46:47.483 line:80%
Why did Yougyum come here?

00:46:48.067 --> 00:46:49.318 line:80%
Is he hurt?

00:46:49.401 --> 00:46:50.611 line:80%
That's personal information.

00:46:50.694 --> 00:46:52.488 line:80%
-[doctor chuckles]
-[♪ music continues]

00:46:53.405 --> 00:46:56.200 line:80%
[sighs] Is she sick or something?

00:46:57.034 --> 00:46:58.035 line:80%
[sighs]

00:46:58.827 --> 00:47:01.121 line:80%
She has to stay healthy.

00:47:05.876 --> 00:47:06.877 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:47:07.711 --> 00:47:09.672 line:80%
-Mmm.
-[Haran gasps]

00:47:09.755 --> 00:47:11.465 line:80%
Hey, you came back.

00:47:11.548 --> 00:47:15.928 line:80%
I finished my first appointment,
so I'm here for the next one with you.

00:47:16.637 --> 00:47:17.638 line:80%
[Chan chuckles]

00:47:18.472 --> 00:47:21.058 line:80%
Seriously, what are we doing here?

00:47:21.141 --> 00:47:22.142 line:80%
You'll see.

00:47:23.227 --> 00:47:26.313 line:80%
KIM SEON POTTERY EXHIBITION

00:47:27.064 --> 00:47:28.524 line:80%
Pottery exhibition?

00:47:29.775 --> 00:47:30.901 line:80%
No way.

00:47:30.985 --> 00:47:32.945 line:80%
-[Chan's grandma] Oh. You're here.
-Grandma!

00:47:34.947 --> 00:47:37.658 line:80%
-Goodness. [exclaims excitedly]
-[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:47:37.741 --> 00:47:39.702 line:80%
-[Chan's grandma] I missed you.
-I feel neglected lately.

00:47:39.785 --> 00:47:40.911 line:80%
-[Chan's grandma] How are you?
-It's okay.

00:47:40.995 --> 00:47:41.996 line:80%
Have you been well?

00:47:42.663 --> 00:47:44.790 line:80%
You should have told me
we were seeing her.

00:47:44.873 --> 00:47:46.709 line:80%
It's not my fault. She told me not to.

00:47:47.584 --> 00:47:49.461 line:80%
If I'd known, I would've gotten flowers--

00:47:49.545 --> 00:47:51.672 line:80%
That's why I told him to keep it secret.

00:47:51.755 --> 00:47:55.843 line:80%
And why would I need flowers
when such a precious guest is here?

00:47:56.593 --> 00:47:57.803 line:80%
Are you two dating?

00:47:58.512 --> 00:47:59.930 line:80%
You little brat.

00:48:00.014 --> 00:48:02.558 line:80%
You should've told me
you were going to the States.

00:48:02.641 --> 00:48:05.352 line:80%
-I was worried when I couldn't reach you.
-I told you.

00:48:05.436 --> 00:48:08.063 line:80%
-I suddenly had to go--
-Still, you should have told her.

00:48:08.147 --> 00:48:09.148 line:80%
Right?

00:48:09.231 --> 00:48:10.941 line:80%
Wow. You're teaming up on me?

00:48:11.025 --> 00:48:12.443 line:80%
That's so mean. I'm leaving.

00:48:12.526 --> 00:48:15.446 line:80%
Come and look around.
And get the cup you made last time.

00:48:15.529 --> 00:48:17.448 line:80%
It looks so beautiful.

00:48:17.531 --> 00:48:20.701 line:80%
[Haran] Really? I'm so excited.
[exclaims excitedly]

00:48:20.784 --> 00:48:22.619 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
My hands look pretty, don't they?

00:48:22.703 --> 00:48:24.913 line:80%
-No one's coming for me? [scoffs]
-[♪ music ends]

00:48:24.997 --> 00:48:26.415 line:80%
I want to be doted on, too!

00:48:40.387 --> 00:48:42.306 line:80%
Oh. This one looks a bit different.

00:48:42.389 --> 00:48:45.934 line:80%
The lines seem pretty rough,
but it's so cool.

00:48:46.018 --> 00:48:48.896 line:80%
The lines are where I mended them.

00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:52.316 line:80%
I put together the shattered pieces.

00:48:52.816 --> 00:48:54.652 line:80%
You can put shattered pieces together?

00:48:54.735 --> 00:48:56.111 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
You know lacquer trees, right?

00:48:56.195 --> 00:48:58.489 line:80%
The sap acts as a natural adhesive.

00:48:59.073 --> 00:49:02.409 line:80%
Once I attach the pieces
and let them dry carefully…

00:49:02.493 --> 00:49:05.871 line:80%
Then they become a new art piece.

00:49:07.706 --> 00:49:11.835 line:80%
They shatter, get hurt, then heal,

00:49:12.461 --> 00:49:14.338 line:80%
and in the process, they gain depth.

00:49:15.589 --> 00:49:17.800 line:80%
It's similar to people, right?

00:49:19.510 --> 00:49:21.178 line:80%
[Chan's grandma chuckles]

00:49:21.261 --> 00:49:25.349 line:80%
Oh… Would it be possible
to restore a broken plate?

00:49:25.432 --> 00:49:28.852 line:80%
It's a dish my mom treasured,
but they don't sell it anymore.

00:49:28.936 --> 00:49:32.189 line:80%
Bring it over sometime.
I'll do my best to restore it.

00:49:32.648 --> 00:49:34.316 line:80%
-[sighs in relief]
-[woman] Ms. Kim.

00:49:34.400 --> 00:49:36.777 line:80%
[exclaims] You're here. Hang on.

00:49:37.361 --> 00:49:38.612 line:80%
Look around.

00:49:38.696 --> 00:49:40.698 line:80%
[women exclaim, lively chatter]

00:49:41.365 --> 00:49:43.283 line:80%
We shouldn't meet like this anymore.

00:49:43.367 --> 00:49:44.576 line:80%
I just get lonely.

00:49:44.660 --> 00:49:45.869 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:49:45.953 --> 00:49:49.248 line:80%
Shouldn't you go and greet them?
They seem like her friends.

00:49:49.331 --> 00:49:51.166 line:80%
Chan, come and say hi.

00:49:51.250 --> 00:49:52.626 line:80%
Okay.

00:49:52.710 --> 00:49:54.211 line:80%
I'll be back soon.

00:49:57.172 --> 00:50:00.259 line:80%
Oh. The kid who visited during vacation?

00:50:00.342 --> 00:50:03.429 line:80%
-Yes.
-You've gotten so handsome!

00:50:03.512 --> 00:50:06.181 line:80%
Thank you.
I turned out pretty well, didn't I?

00:50:06.265 --> 00:50:08.851 line:80%
Oh my. Look how cheeky he's gotten.

00:50:08.934 --> 00:50:10.352 line:80%
[grandmas chuckle]

00:50:10.436 --> 00:50:12.146 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>You used to call him Chan.</i>

00:50:12.229 --> 00:50:15.065 line:80%
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

00:50:15.816 --> 00:50:17.192 line:80%
Seonu Chan?

00:50:19.153 --> 00:50:20.279 line:80%
Seonu…

00:50:21.113 --> 00:50:22.156 line:80%
Chan.

00:50:22.656 --> 00:50:24.491 line:80%
[♪ mellow music plays]

00:50:26.702 --> 00:50:28.162 line:80%
[Chan's grandma] He's shameless, like me.

00:50:28.245 --> 00:50:30.039 line:80%
[all laugh]

00:50:35.794 --> 00:50:37.796 line:80%
Oh? There's no one here.

00:50:37.880 --> 00:50:39.423 line:80%
Everyone went home.

00:50:39.506 --> 00:50:40.924 line:80%
Is Hayeong not here?

00:50:41.008 --> 00:50:43.344 line:80%
We were going to discuss
the new material today.

00:50:43.427 --> 00:50:46.138 line:80%
She was feeble all day,
unlike her usual self,

00:50:46.221 --> 00:50:47.598 line:80%
and went home early.

00:50:47.681 --> 00:50:49.099 line:80%
Try calling her.

00:50:49.183 --> 00:50:50.184 line:80%
Bye, then.

00:50:55.773 --> 00:50:56.982 line:80%
[line connects, rings]

00:50:57.066 --> 00:50:58.734 line:80%
Ms. Song.

00:50:58.817 --> 00:50:59.902 line:80%
[man] <i>Hello?</i>

00:50:59.985 --> 00:51:01.737 line:80%
<i>Are you a friend of hers?</i>

00:51:02.946 --> 00:51:05.741 line:80%
<i>She's been drinking and sleeping nonstop.</i>

00:51:05.824 --> 00:51:07.576 line:80%
<i>You should come and take her home.</i>

00:51:08.410 --> 00:51:10.412 line:80%
[♪ upbeat music playing over speakers]

00:51:20.589 --> 00:51:21.590 line:80%
Ah. [laughs]

00:51:22.216 --> 00:51:24.301 line:80%
Good morning.

00:51:24.885 --> 00:51:26.387 line:80%
When did I come to work, though?

00:51:26.470 --> 00:51:28.639 line:80%
You got off work. This is a wine bar.

00:51:28.722 --> 00:51:30.224 line:80%
I'll take you home.

00:51:30.307 --> 00:51:33.185 line:80%
What? To where? Home?

00:51:33.268 --> 00:51:35.396 line:80%
[groans] No, I can't.

00:51:36.397 --> 00:51:38.565 line:80%
I can't face Hadam.

00:51:41.318 --> 00:51:44.905 line:80%
I should have told her more
about Mom and Dad.

00:51:45.864 --> 00:51:48.200 line:80%
I should have known how she felt.

00:51:49.243 --> 00:51:51.704 line:80%
I should have known

00:51:52.496 --> 00:51:54.540 line:80%
so no one would get hurt.

00:51:56.291 --> 00:51:59.962 line:80%
Hadam was only six at the time.

00:52:00.045 --> 00:52:03.966 line:80%
But she was in the car with Mom and Dad

00:52:04.758 --> 00:52:06.176 line:80%
during…

00:52:07.052 --> 00:52:08.846 line:80%
the accident…

00:52:10.514 --> 00:52:12.516 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:52:22.443 --> 00:52:23.569 line:80%
It's cold.

00:52:48.594 --> 00:52:49.595 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:52:55.392 --> 00:52:56.935 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:53:01.065 --> 00:53:04.485 line:80%
It's just that you were crying…

00:53:04.985 --> 00:53:08.030 line:80%
[exclaims] It's just drool.

00:53:08.739 --> 00:53:11.742 line:80%
[stutters] Let's go.

00:53:11.825 --> 00:53:13.702 line:80%
-All right.
-[Hayeong clears throat]

00:53:15.871 --> 00:53:17.039 line:80%
The GPS…

00:53:19.750 --> 00:53:21.210 line:80%
Wait.

00:53:21.293 --> 00:53:22.503 line:80%
Seongsu-dong?

00:53:22.586 --> 00:53:23.587 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:53:30.344 --> 00:53:31.762 line:80%
Was I mistaken?

00:53:32.888 --> 00:53:36.475 line:80%
Did you go to Seongsu-dong last Thursday?

00:53:37.518 --> 00:53:39.144 line:80%
You were with Grandma, right?

00:53:39.812 --> 00:53:41.814 line:80%
-No. I'll start the car.
-Wait.

00:53:41.897 --> 00:53:43.732 line:80%
I saw Grandma that day.

00:53:43.816 --> 00:53:46.026 line:80%
I'm sure I saw her crying.

00:53:46.902 --> 00:53:48.737 line:80%
She was crying?

00:53:48.821 --> 00:53:50.614 line:80%
So you did go to Seongsu-dong, right?

00:53:52.616 --> 00:53:54.326 line:80%
[sighs] That woke me right up.

00:53:56.662 --> 00:53:57.788 line:80%
Is something going on?

00:53:59.373 --> 00:54:00.749 line:80%
What is it?

00:54:00.833 --> 00:54:03.168 line:80%
I'm sorry, but just let this go for now.

00:54:04.503 --> 00:54:05.671 line:80%
Please.

00:54:15.097 --> 00:54:17.099 line:80%
[♪ somber music playing]

00:54:30.863 --> 00:54:33.157 line:20%
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

00:54:33.240 --> 00:54:34.241 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:54:38.287 --> 00:54:40.706 line:80%
You can't stop looking at it.
Are you that impressed?

00:54:40.789 --> 00:54:42.499 line:80%
Are you sure I really made this?

00:54:42.583 --> 00:54:44.501 line:80%
Did you make it again
because it was a mess?

00:54:44.585 --> 00:54:46.420 line:80%
-Of course not.
-[both laugh]

00:54:47.129 --> 00:54:51.008 line:80%
I'd love to have dinner with you,
but I'm meeting the people who helped me.

00:54:51.091 --> 00:54:54.386 line:80%
I'll stay in Seoul for a few days,
so let's have a meal sometime.

00:54:54.470 --> 00:54:56.513 line:80%
And bring your mother's dish then.

00:54:56.597 --> 00:54:57.890 line:80%
All right.

00:54:57.973 --> 00:55:00.267 line:80%
Her mother's dish? What do you mean?

00:55:00.351 --> 00:55:02.519 line:80%
-Why are you curious about everything?
-[groans]

00:55:02.603 --> 00:55:04.938 line:80%
Grandma, don't do that in front of her.

00:55:05.022 --> 00:55:06.357 line:80%
-[Chan groans]
-Your cheeks are so squishy.

00:55:06.440 --> 00:55:07.441 line:80%
[Haran and Chan's grandma chuckle]

00:55:10.069 --> 00:55:11.403 line:80%
The weather's so nice.

00:55:11.987 --> 00:55:13.155 line:80%
How about dinner--

00:55:13.238 --> 00:55:15.032 line:80%
Sorry, but you should go home first.

00:55:15.741 --> 00:55:17.743 line:80%
-I'll see you later.
-Where are you going?

00:55:18.285 --> 00:55:19.536 line:80%
Ms. Song!

00:55:21.538 --> 00:55:24.291 line:80%
Being overly polite
will hurt her feelings.

00:55:24.375 --> 00:55:27.002 line:80%
But I should at least give her
some hand lotion.

00:55:28.671 --> 00:55:29.672 line:80%
Huh?

00:55:34.426 --> 00:55:36.011 line:80%
Oh? Did she leave?

00:55:37.513 --> 00:55:38.514 line:80%
Hang on.

00:55:42.059 --> 00:55:43.852 line:80%
-She's not here?
-Did she leave?

00:55:43.936 --> 00:55:45.270 line:80%
We can come back…

00:55:45.354 --> 00:55:46.355 line:80%
[exclaims softly]

00:55:47.731 --> 00:55:48.732 line:80%
Hmm?

00:55:48.816 --> 00:55:50.818 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:55:55.239 --> 00:55:56.907 line:80%
[young Chan] <i>Dad. Dad!</i>

00:55:56.991 --> 00:55:59.034 line:80%
[Chan's dad] <i>What more do I have to do</i>
<i>to make you stop?</i>

00:56:04.039 --> 00:56:05.374 line:80%
Let's just go.

00:56:05.457 --> 00:56:07.835 line:80%
-Wait, I…
-[Chan's dad] Chan.

00:56:12.214 --> 00:56:14.216 line:80%
[chuckles awkwardly] You're back.

00:56:14.883 --> 00:56:17.845 line:80%
He had business nearby

00:56:17.928 --> 00:56:21.598 line:80%
and dropped by to greet me
when he saw the sign.

00:56:22.599 --> 00:56:24.101 line:80%
[Chan's dad inhales sharply, hesitates]

00:56:24.852 --> 00:56:25.978 line:80%
It's been a while.

00:56:28.272 --> 00:56:31.150 line:80%
There was
an international conference nearby.

00:56:31.233 --> 00:56:32.234 line:80%
Your school…

00:56:32.901 --> 00:56:37.072 line:80%
No, your former school
and some other schools--

00:56:37.156 --> 00:56:38.741 line:80%
That's enough.

00:56:38.824 --> 00:56:40.242 line:80%
I'm not even curious.

00:56:41.952 --> 00:56:43.704 line:80%
-Let's go.
-How are you?

00:56:44.371 --> 00:56:46.457 line:80%
How is your condition these days?

00:56:50.336 --> 00:56:53.213 line:80%
[door opens, closes]

00:56:55.424 --> 00:56:56.550 line:80%
Are you going somewhere?

00:57:00.054 --> 00:57:01.388 line:80%
Why are you taking your passport?

00:57:02.222 --> 00:57:03.849 line:80%
I don't want to stay in Korea.

00:57:04.433 --> 00:57:06.185 line:80%
You made a good decision.

00:57:07.311 --> 00:57:11.065 line:80%
You received enough treatment,
so you can return to school--

00:57:11.148 --> 00:57:12.566 line:80%
I'm not…

00:57:13.567 --> 00:57:14.818 line:80%
going back to school.

00:57:14.902 --> 00:57:16.195 line:80%
I'm not studying anymore.

00:57:17.696 --> 00:57:19.865 line:80%
What? You've already wasted so much time.

00:57:20.866 --> 00:57:24.286 line:80%
Are you going to give up everything
just because of some accident?

00:57:24.787 --> 00:57:28.248 line:80%
Stop acting like a child
and be reasonable.

00:57:28.332 --> 00:57:31.669 line:80%
You should finish your master's
and move on to a PhD program…

00:57:32.294 --> 00:57:33.629 line:80%
Do you not see me?

00:57:35.214 --> 00:57:39.009 line:80%
I'm covered in burn scars,
and I can't hear on one side.

00:57:39.968 --> 00:57:42.388 line:80%
-You call that "some accident"?
-It's in the past.

00:57:42.888 --> 00:57:44.431 line:80%
Blaming it won't change anything.

00:57:44.515 --> 00:57:46.934 line:80%
Enough with the pathetic self-pity!

00:57:47.851 --> 00:57:48.852 line:80%
[scoffs lightly]

00:57:50.270 --> 00:57:51.605 line:80%
[sighs]

00:57:51.689 --> 00:57:52.773 line:80%
I get it now.

00:57:53.607 --> 00:57:57.027 line:80%
This is why she left you.
It was because of you.

00:57:57.111 --> 00:57:58.862 line:80%
She didn't just leave,

00:57:59.697 --> 00:58:01.115 line:80%
you made her leave!

00:58:01.198 --> 00:58:02.950 line:80%
I'll leave too.

00:58:03.033 --> 00:58:04.743 line:80%
I'll live my own life,

00:58:05.285 --> 00:58:08.831 line:80%
so just think
that your stupid, obedient son…

00:58:08.914 --> 00:58:09.915 line:80%
[sighs]

00:58:11.625 --> 00:58:12.751 line:80%
died…

00:58:13.961 --> 00:58:15.879 line:80%
in that explosion.

00:58:17.548 --> 00:58:18.549 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:58:19.133 --> 00:58:20.342 line:80%
[sighs]

00:58:23.554 --> 00:58:24.805 line:80%
Why are you acting like this?

00:58:24.888 --> 00:58:27.266 line:80%
You never worried about me before.

00:58:27.349 --> 00:58:29.393 line:80%
[♪ somber music playing]

00:58:30.019 --> 00:58:31.854 line:80%
I saw you here earlier,

00:58:32.563 --> 00:58:36.358 line:80%
so I left,
in case you'd feel uncomfortable.

00:58:37.818 --> 00:58:39.695 line:80%
I didn't know you'd come back.

00:58:39.778 --> 00:58:40.863 line:80%
You're right.

00:58:41.488 --> 00:58:43.073 line:80%
I do feel uncomfortable.

00:58:43.157 --> 00:58:46.618 line:80%
So if you ever see me anywhere again,

00:58:47.161 --> 00:58:48.162 line:80%
don't even say hi.

00:58:48.245 --> 00:58:49.955 line:80%
Chan, don't do this!

00:58:50.039 --> 00:58:52.541 line:80%
Are you going to keep acting
like you're strangers?

00:58:52.624 --> 00:58:54.543 line:80%
Since you've met… Hmm?

00:58:55.336 --> 00:58:57.004 line:80%
Give her the flowers. I'm leaving.

00:58:58.797 --> 00:59:00.424 line:80%
-Chan, let's talk--
-Stop!

00:59:00.507 --> 00:59:02.051 line:80%
[Chan's grandma screams]

00:59:02.134 --> 00:59:03.427 line:80%
[gasps]

00:59:03.510 --> 00:59:05.095 line:80%
[Chan breathing heavily]

00:59:06.388 --> 00:59:07.681 line:80%
[exhales heavily]

00:59:07.765 --> 00:59:10.768 line:80%
[grunts angrily]

00:59:12.436 --> 00:59:14.438 line:80%
[breath trembling]

00:59:16.565 --> 00:59:17.858 line:80%
Chan! Don't. Stop.

00:59:17.941 --> 00:59:19.735 line:80%
Let him go! Let go of him!

00:59:19.818 --> 00:59:20.903 line:80%
Let him go.

00:59:20.986 --> 00:59:22.404 line:80%
Don't do this!

00:59:22.488 --> 00:59:24.782 line:80%
Chan, let him go!

00:59:24.865 --> 00:59:27.910 line:80%
Go. Everyone, just go!

00:59:36.251 --> 00:59:37.711 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:59:39.213 --> 00:59:41.048 line:80%
Oh, dear. Let me see.

00:59:41.674 --> 00:59:42.966 line:80%
Oh, no.

00:59:43.425 --> 00:59:44.426 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:59:44.510 --> 00:59:47.721 line:80%
[breathes heavily] It's okay.
I didn't even notice. I'm really fine.

00:59:48.764 --> 00:59:51.684 line:80%
Grandma, take care of her for me.

00:59:53.352 --> 00:59:54.812 line:80%
Wait…

00:59:56.647 --> 00:59:57.940 line:80%
He won't be able…

00:59:59.191 --> 01:00:00.985 line:80%
to face you right now.

01:00:03.112 --> 01:00:04.780 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

01:00:05.572 --> 01:00:06.782 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

01:00:06.865 --> 01:00:08.200 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

01:00:19.253 --> 01:00:21.505 line:80%
Darn it…

01:00:30.264 --> 01:00:31.265 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:00:32.391 --> 01:00:34.059 line:80%
[Chan's grandma sighs]

01:00:34.143 --> 01:00:36.687 line:80%
I'll be able to fix the shattered pottery,

01:00:38.188 --> 01:00:41.233 line:80%
but I can't do anything
about their relationship.

01:00:42.234 --> 01:00:44.695 line:80%
They've had a deep rift for a long time.

01:00:46.196 --> 01:00:48.198 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

01:00:49.199 --> 01:00:50.784 line:80%
You can take it.

01:00:50.868 --> 01:00:52.536 line:80%
Sorry, hang on.

01:00:53.162 --> 01:00:54.496 line:80%
Yes, Director.

01:00:55.497 --> 01:00:56.498 line:80%
Yes.

01:00:56.582 --> 01:00:58.208 line:80%
Of course.

01:01:07.051 --> 01:01:09.845 line:20%
PROFESSOR SUNWOO SEOK

01:01:10.721 --> 01:01:12.097 line:20%
[Haran] "Science University"?

01:01:12.890 --> 01:01:14.350 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

01:01:14.433 --> 01:01:15.726 line:80%
[Chan] <i>From the smell,</i>

01:01:15.809 --> 01:01:18.145 line:80%
it seemed like
diluted sodium hypochlorite solution.

01:01:18.228 --> 01:01:20.898 line:80%
Because of the diffraction of sunlight,
the cloud particles…

01:01:21.398 --> 01:01:22.858 line:80%
Petrichor.

01:01:23.484 --> 01:01:25.569 line:80%
[Seok] <i>Your former school</i>
<i>and some other schools…</i>

01:01:25.653 --> 01:01:27.237 line:80%
[officer] <i>I guess</i>
<i>you majored in that field.</i>

01:01:27.321 --> 01:01:29.281 line:80%
[Haran] <i>It seems like</i>
<i>you majored in engineering.</i>

01:01:29.365 --> 01:01:31.700 line:80%
[Ben] <i>He never tells me</i>
<i>what he did before entering CalArts.</i>

01:01:31.784 --> 01:01:33.494 line:80%
I lived like a corpse.

01:01:43.754 --> 01:01:44.838 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:01:44.922 --> 01:01:45.923 line:80%
[knock on door]

01:01:46.924 --> 01:01:49.301 line:80%
Laundry…

01:01:49.385 --> 01:01:50.636 line:80%
Is there any laundry?

01:01:52.012 --> 01:01:53.138 line:80%
[object clatters]

01:01:55.516 --> 01:01:56.642 line:80%
[grunts]

01:02:00.604 --> 01:02:02.731 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:02:04.358 --> 01:02:06.819 line:80%
What happened to the pen you always use?

01:02:06.902 --> 01:02:08.779 line:80%
I lost it, and I never found it.

01:02:08.862 --> 01:02:10.364 line:80%
I'll just use a new one now.

01:02:11.240 --> 01:02:12.574 line:80%
[Chan] It's nothing special.

01:02:13.784 --> 01:02:14.785 line:80%
Wait.

01:02:15.494 --> 01:02:17.538 line:80%
Why is this pen here?

01:02:18.080 --> 01:02:19.081 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:02:23.335 --> 01:02:24.878 line:80%
Huh? Genius.

01:02:26.005 --> 01:02:27.006 line:80%
[sighs]

01:02:30.259 --> 01:02:31.760 line:80%
Mr. Seonu.

01:02:32.636 --> 01:02:34.179 line:80%
Oh? You're in here.

01:02:34.263 --> 01:02:36.432 line:80%
Yes, I was collecting laundry.

01:02:36.515 --> 01:02:38.892 line:80%
But why did you come upstairs?

01:02:38.976 --> 01:02:40.936 line:80%
Sorry, I came without asking.

01:02:41.020 --> 01:02:43.981 line:80%
I just wanted to see Mr. Seonu.
I have something to give him.

01:02:44.064 --> 01:02:45.983 line:80%
He hasn't come home yet.

01:02:46.066 --> 01:02:47.568 line:80%
Let's go. I'll make you coffee.

01:02:47.651 --> 01:02:49.236 line:80%
-Okay.
-All right.

01:02:51.780 --> 01:02:53.073 line:80%
What happened?

01:02:53.907 --> 01:02:55.242 line:80%
Did you get hurt?

01:02:55.326 --> 01:02:57.036 line:80%
It's just a small scratch.

01:02:57.119 --> 01:02:58.245 line:80%
[toy] <i>Let's go on a walk.</i>

01:02:58.329 --> 01:03:00.205 line:80%
<i>Let's go on a walk.</i>

01:03:00.289 --> 01:03:03.083 line:80%
[exclaims] We didn't get to go
on a walk today.

01:03:03.167 --> 01:03:05.294 line:80%
You can go. I don't need coffee.

01:03:05.377 --> 01:03:07.212 line:80%
I'll wait here for Mr. Seonu.

01:03:07.296 --> 01:03:08.339 line:80%
Are you sure?

01:03:09.715 --> 01:03:11.216 line:80%
Hey, Haran…

01:03:11.300 --> 01:03:13.761 line:80%
About before…

01:03:14.803 --> 01:03:16.180 line:80%
[hesitates] No, never mind.

01:03:16.764 --> 01:03:18.474 line:80%
I'll be back soon.

01:03:18.557 --> 01:03:19.767 line:80%
Wait a moment.

01:03:20.309 --> 01:03:23.604 line:80%
cafe SHIM

01:03:24.188 --> 01:03:25.189 line:80%
[sighs softly]

01:03:26.982 --> 01:03:28.317 line:80%
Why isn't he coming?

01:03:33.447 --> 01:03:34.698 line:80%
Oh?

01:03:34.782 --> 01:03:35.783 line:80%
You're here.

01:03:39.787 --> 01:03:41.789 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

01:03:44.958 --> 01:03:46.919 line:80%
[sighs] Where have you been this whole…

01:03:48.504 --> 01:03:50.881 line:80%
Let's go inside. You look exhausted.

01:03:50.964 --> 01:03:52.299 line:80%
[Chan] I'm sorry.

01:03:52.883 --> 01:03:54.426 line:80%
For leaving like that

01:03:55.302 --> 01:03:57.137 line:80%
and for hurting you.

01:03:58.722 --> 01:03:59.932 line:80%
It's okay.

01:04:00.933 --> 01:04:02.518 line:80%
I'm totally fine.

01:04:04.019 --> 01:04:05.229 line:80%
It's all my fault.

01:04:05.771 --> 01:04:10.359 line:80%
I was being selfish,
trying to stay by your side.

01:04:10.442 --> 01:04:11.527 line:80%
What are you saying?

01:04:12.194 --> 01:04:14.571 line:80%
Just make me some tea
instead of saying such nonsense.

01:04:19.994 --> 01:04:21.078 line:80%
[sighs]

01:04:28.419 --> 01:04:29.420 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:04:30.587 --> 01:04:32.589 line:80%
I've been thinking…

01:04:33.632 --> 01:04:38.470 line:80%
I don't think it's a good idea
for us to be this close, so--

01:04:38.554 --> 01:04:39.805 line:80%
You saw this, right?

01:04:40.431 --> 01:04:42.850 line:80%
Wow. I was so surprised when I saw it.

01:04:44.018 --> 01:04:47.521 line:80%
These lines are where she mended
the broken pieces.

01:04:47.604 --> 01:04:49.940 line:80%
Don't they make this look more beautiful?

01:04:50.691 --> 01:04:53.319 line:80%
It seems admirable, too.

01:04:53.902 --> 01:04:55.779 line:80%
-Ms. Song.
-To me…

01:04:58.741 --> 01:05:00.159 line:80%
you're these lines.

01:05:01.035 --> 01:05:02.953 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

01:05:03.037 --> 01:05:04.330 line:80%
[Chan] Ms. Song!

01:05:07.249 --> 01:05:08.625 line:80%
[Haran] <i>The first snow…</i>

01:05:10.002 --> 01:05:11.086 line:80%
<i>Vapor trails…</i>

01:05:11.170 --> 01:05:12.963 line:80%
Wow, it's beautiful.

01:05:13.756 --> 01:05:15.257 line:80%
<i>Jamsugyo…</i>

01:05:16.008 --> 01:05:18.218 line:80%
<i>And a certain name…</i>

01:05:19.136 --> 01:05:22.556 line:80%
<i>They were all sad memories,</i>
<i>so I thought I'd never get over them.</i>

01:05:23.307 --> 01:05:26.226 line:80%
<i>But I found myself feeling okay,</i>

01:05:27.227 --> 01:05:28.896 line:80%
thanks to someone

01:05:29.897 --> 01:05:32.149 line:80%
who covered them with good memories.

01:05:32.483 --> 01:05:33.567 line:80%
[sighs]

01:05:33.651 --> 01:05:37.196 line:80%
But you say something like that
over a tiny scratch?

01:05:37.321 --> 01:05:38.322 line:80%
[scoffs]

01:05:39.073 --> 01:05:41.241 line:80%
It's a relief I met you here.

01:05:42.993 --> 01:05:45.204 line:80%
Thanks to you, I found a way,

01:05:45.788 --> 01:05:49.249 line:80%
so this time, why don't you try it…

01:05:51.210 --> 01:05:52.252 line:80%
with your father?

01:05:55.130 --> 01:05:56.548 line:80%
That's impossible.

01:05:59.593 --> 01:06:01.387 line:80%
You remember when we first met, right?

01:06:02.221 --> 01:06:05.057 line:80%
I was cold and avoided you.

01:06:05.849 --> 01:06:08.394 line:80%
I thought it was impossible too.

01:06:08.978 --> 01:06:13.148 line:80%
But I guess there's no such thing
as never in a relationship.

01:06:13.899 --> 01:06:16.610 line:80%
Aren't I a good example of that?

01:06:22.282 --> 01:06:24.243 line:80%
I picked this up at the exhibit.

01:06:25.911 --> 01:06:27.830 line:20%
He must wear this all the time.

01:06:27.913 --> 01:06:29.498 line:20%
It's in the photo as well.

01:06:33.919 --> 01:06:35.045 line:80%
I've never seen it before.

01:06:35.129 --> 01:06:36.338 line:80%
Really?

01:06:37.214 --> 01:06:40.884 line:80%
The drawing here looks similar
to the one I saw at your grandma's place.

01:06:46.181 --> 01:06:47.391 line:80%
[sighs]

01:06:47.474 --> 01:06:51.312 line:80%
[Haran] He must have kept wearing it
even when it was broken.

01:06:53.397 --> 01:06:55.232 line:80%
I bought that for him a long time ago

01:06:56.358 --> 01:06:58.027 line:80%
at a stationary store

01:06:59.236 --> 01:07:00.696 line:80%
for Parents' Day.

01:07:01.655 --> 01:07:02.948 line:80%
Maybe…

01:07:03.782 --> 01:07:05.951 line:80%
he wanted to mend things.

01:07:06.535 --> 01:07:09.163 line:80%
He's been wearing this broken watch
the whole time.

01:07:11.707 --> 01:07:12.708 line:80%
[sighs]

01:07:13.375 --> 01:07:14.376 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:07:19.757 --> 01:07:20.799 line:80%
[sighs]

01:07:21.592 --> 01:07:23.552 line:80%
[sighs] I should give you some time alone.

01:07:28.474 --> 01:07:29.642 line:80%
Thank you.

01:07:34.605 --> 01:07:36.607 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:07:37.149 --> 01:07:38.359 line:80%
[Haran sighs]

01:07:38.442 --> 01:07:43.238 line:80%
I have a habit
of hugging people I want to comfort.

01:07:44.448 --> 01:07:46.033 line:80%
That's my thing.

01:07:47.534 --> 01:07:48.869 line:80%
Why do you keep copying me?

01:07:52.289 --> 01:07:55.042 line:80%
I wish we'd met earlier.

01:07:55.918 --> 01:07:59.004 line:80%
Then we could've gotten close faster,
and I would've been nicer first.

01:08:00.464 --> 01:08:02.966 line:80%
I would have at least given you a hug

01:08:03.050 --> 01:08:05.928 line:80%
when you were scared to open your eyes.

01:08:10.224 --> 01:08:11.684 line:80%
[Chan sighs wearily]

01:08:11.767 --> 01:08:14.853 line:80%
[laptop pinging]

01:08:15.437 --> 01:08:18.732 line:80%
[Chan] <i>You saved me as well.</i>

01:08:18.816 --> 01:08:20.526 line:80%
[rain pattering]

01:08:26.115 --> 01:08:29.451 line:80%
You already did that for me.

01:08:35.833 --> 01:08:36.834 line:80%
[sighs]

01:08:36.917 --> 01:08:37.918 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:08:46.093 --> 01:08:51.682 line:80%
[Chan] Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

01:08:52.474 --> 01:08:56.979 line:80%
The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

01:08:57.062 --> 01:08:58.814 line:80%
Her boyfriend died back then.

01:08:58.897 --> 01:09:01.400 line:80%
He went to study in Boston,
but he suddenly died.

01:09:01.483 --> 01:09:03.485 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:09:06.739 --> 01:09:10.743 line:80%
[in English] "Newbury Street, Boston?"

01:09:18.459 --> 01:09:19.460 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:09:20.294 --> 01:09:22.171 line:80%
[in Korean] I've only
received things from you.

01:09:26.175 --> 01:09:28.093 line:80%
I should be really nice to you
from now on.

01:09:31.805 --> 01:09:32.848 line:80%
Then…

01:09:35.768 --> 01:09:37.519 line:80%
I might end up liking you even more.

01:09:38.145 --> 01:09:39.688 line:80%
It's okay…

01:09:41.023 --> 01:09:42.149 line:80%
if you like me more.

01:09:44.318 --> 01:09:45.527 line:80%
If I like you more…

01:09:49.406 --> 01:09:50.866 line:80%
I might get more greedy.

01:09:54.370 --> 01:09:55.412 line:80%
It's okay

01:09:56.664 --> 01:09:58.123 line:80%
if you get more greedy.

01:10:06.131 --> 01:10:08.092 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:10:50.843 --> 01:10:52.761 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:10:52.845 --> 01:10:54.847 line:20%
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

01:11:16.869 --> 01:11:20.914 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Why do you keep saying</i>
<i>it's greedy to like me?</i>

01:11:20.998 --> 01:11:23.375 line:20%
-[Manjae] <i>You mean it, right?</i>
-[Chan] <i>Yes.</i>

01:11:23.459 --> 01:11:27.463 line:20%
[Haran] <i>How about letting time</i>
<i>with your dad start moving again?</i>

01:11:27.546 --> 01:11:29.381 line:20%
<i>The past is the past,</i>

01:11:29.465 --> 01:11:32.843 line:20%
<i>and what matters is the time you have now.</i>

01:11:32.926 --> 01:11:35.387 line:20%
[Hayeong]
<i>There's nothing wrong with her, right?</i>

01:11:35.471 --> 01:11:38.766 line:20%
[Manjae]
<i>What on earth is happening to you?</i>

01:11:38.849 --> 01:11:41.727 line:20%
[Chan] <i>Seonu Chan found this pen for you.</i>

01:11:41.810 --> 01:11:44.188 line:20%
<i>And this is a lucky charm.</i>

01:11:44.271 --> 01:11:47.107 line:20%
[Haran] <i>No way. What is this?</i>

01:11:51.111 --> 01:11:52.112 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

01:11:53.197 --> 01:11:55.199 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

01:12:01.080 --> 01:12:02.081 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:12:02.164 --> 01:12:03.165 line:80%
Translated by Juyoung Park